Notebook[{
Cell["Quantum Optics with QuantumInterferometer", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
Beam splitters, coherent light, multiphoton interference, squeezed states, \
attenuation, waveguide arrays, and conditional optical gates: a \
computation-first tour with the Wolfram Language.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: October 26, 2026)", "Text",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Introduction: from optical inputs to measured outputs", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["\<\
These fourteen experiments connect optical inputs to photon-counting \
probabilities, coherent amplitudes, and conditional states. Each calculation \
tests a physical prediction. Start a fresh Wolfram Language kernel and \
evaluate the cells in order; later examples reuse earlier definitions. Change \
the inputs and parameters to explore the results.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["Prerequisites and setup", "Subsection",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Basic complex numbers, matrices, and quantum states are assumed. A ",
 StyleBox["mode",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is an independent optical field component, such as a spatial path. A ",
 StyleBox["Fock state",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " has definite photon numbers. Its ",
 StyleBox["occupation pattern",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 ", lists the photon number in each mode. A ",
 StyleBox["coherent state",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " has a complex coherent amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " and mean photon number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 ". We assume ideal photon-number-resolving detectors throughout."
}], "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumInterferometer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " (QI) represents beam splitters, phase shifters, squeezers, and pure-loss \
channels. Lossless passive networks conserve photon number and have a unitary \
transfer matrix. Their Fock-state transition amplitudes are normalized \
permanents; squeezed-network amplitudes use hafnians. Lossy probabilities sum \
over the unobserved environment outcomes. QI applies pure loss directly to \
probabilities and finite states."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell["\<\
Individual transition queries need no Fock-space cutoff. Listing \
coherent-state or squeezed-state probabilities requires a total photon-number \
cutoff. A Fock-space circuit or channel instead requires a number of levels \
per mode. Lossless passive transition queries accept symbolic occupations. \
With loss, symbolic occupations are supported for independent attenuators; \
mode mixing requires explicit occupations. Squeezed networks require explicit \
occupations but allow symbolic squeezing parameters.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Symbolic formulas retain their physical domains. Use ",
 Cell[BoxData["Assumptions"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " in a transition query or ",
 Cell[BoxData["Refine"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " to display a formula on a specified domain. Bare beam splitters act on \
modes 1 and 2; bare phase shifters, squeezers, and loss elements act on mode \
1. The default beam splitter phase is zero, and the mode count is inferred \
from the elements."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell["Load the quantum-state and operator tools:", "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell["Load the second-quantization tools:", "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"",
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell["\<\
Conventions: transfer matrices, beam splitter phases, and mode ordering\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a lossless passive network, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox["1", 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]]},
     "Bra"], 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox["1", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 ": column ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 " gives the single-photon amplitudes for input mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 ". We use ",
 StyleBox["transmissivity",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["reflectivity",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 ". These are probabilities; transmission and reflection amplitudes also \
carry phases. Beam splitter angles and phase shifts are real; coherent \
amplitudes may be complex. A phase shifter contributes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"i", "\[Phi]"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " per photon."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell["Build a beam splitter with zero reflection phase:", "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"conventionBS", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell["Draw the beam splitter with its parameters:", "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"conventionBS", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell["Read its transfer matrix:", "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"conventionBS", "[", "\"\<Unitary\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The reflected amplitudes have opposite real signs. A reflection phase of ",
 Cell["\\[Pi]/2", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 " gives the symmetric convention used in many textbooks. Build that beam \
splitter:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"symmetricConventionBS", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell["Draw the beam splitter in the symmetric convention:", "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"symmetricConventionBS", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell["Read its transfer matrix:", "Text",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"symmetricConventionBS", "[", "\"\<Unitary\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell["\<\
The symmetric convention has imaginary reflection amplitudes. We state any \
convention change explicitly; some texts also reverse the phase-shift sign. \
All optical parameters here are dimensionless. Waveguide propagation lengths \
are measured in inverse coupling units.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],

Cell["Part I: Optical components and photon statistics", "Section",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell["\<\
1. Two-photon interference: indistinguishability and coincidences\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Send one photon into each input mode. Assume the photons have identical \
polarization, spectrum, and temporal shape. At a balanced beam splitter, the \
two amplitudes for one photon in each output cancel. Both photons leave in \
the same output mode: the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect. Distinguishable photons \
instead have coincidence probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build a beam splitter with symbolic angle ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Theta]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 " and reflection phase ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Phi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hom", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell["Draw the beam splitter:", "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hom", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the output Fock-state amplitudes for one photon in each input:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"hom", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coincidence outcome is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 ". Compute its probability with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["FullSimplify",
   BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
   ButtonData->{
     URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/FullSimplify.html"], 
     None}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 ", assuming real parameters:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"hom", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "|", " ", "\[Phi]"}], ")"}], " ", "\[Element]",
      " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 ", independent of the reflection phase. Build the balanced beam splitter at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"balanced", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell["Draw the balanced beam splitter:", "Text",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell["\<\
The coincidence amplitude vanishes. Compute the two surviving bunching \
amplitudes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell["\<\
Indistinguishable alternatives interfere as amplitudes. Distinguishable \
alternatives contribute separate probabilities. Verify the indistinguishable \
coincidence probability:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell["For the distinguishable reference, read the transfer matrix:", "Text",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"balancedMatrix", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", "\"\<Unitary\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell["\<\
Add the probabilities for both photons being transmitted or both being \
reflected:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"balancedMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"balancedMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
   "+", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"balancedMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"balancedMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], 
  " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell["\<\
Distinguishability restores coincidences. A delay scan requires a model of \
the temporal overlap, which is absent from these fixed-mode inputs.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reference:", "TI"],
 " C. K. Hong, Z. Y. Ou, L. Mandel, Phys. Rev. Lett. ",
 StyleBox["59",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 2044 (1987)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],

Cell["2. Optical meshes: three realizations of one unitary", "Subsection",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A lossless passive network on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " modes has an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 " unitary transfer matrix. Beam splitters and phase shifters can realize it \
in several layouts: triangular Reck, rectangular Clements, or recursive \
cosine-sine meshes. Compare their component counts, depths, and \
reconstruction errors."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell["Set a reproducible random seed:", "Text",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "6", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell["Generate a six-mode Haar-random target unitary:", "Text",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"targetUnitary", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"CircularUnitaryMatrixDistribution", "[", "6", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],

Cell["Decompose the target into the three meshes:", "Text",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"meshes", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
      RowBox[{"targetUnitary", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
    "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Clements\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Reck\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<CosineSine\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell["Draw the three meshes:", "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Labeled", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#2", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "#1", ",", " ", 
       "Top"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "meshes"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell["Count the beam splitters in each mesh:", "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<BeamSplitterCount\>\"", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
   " ", "meshes"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell["Depth counts beam splitter layers. Compare the mesh depths:", "Text",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<Depth\>\"", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
   "meshes"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell["\<\
Check the decomposition by rebuilding each mesh from its optical elements. \
This tests the elements rather than the stored target matrix. Build the \
reconstructed networks:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"rebuiltMeshes", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<Elements\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], 
     " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "meshes"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell["Draw the reconstructed meshes:", "Text",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Labeled", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#2", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "#1", ",", " ", 
       "Top"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "rebuiltMeshes"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Chop",
   BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
   ButtonData->{
     URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Chop.html"], None}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " replaces small numerical residuals with zero. Compute the largest \
matrix-entry error for each reconstruction:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<Unitary\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        "targetUnitary"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
   "rebuiltMeshes"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell["\<\
All three meshes reproduce the target. The Clements mesh uses the fewest \
layers in this example.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["References:", "TI"],
 " M. Reck et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. ",
 StyleBox["73",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 58 (1994); W. R. Clements et al., Optica ",
 StyleBox["3",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 1460 (2016); I. Dhand, S. K. Goyal, Phys. Rev. A ",
 StyleBox["92",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 043813 (2015)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell["3. Fourier multiports: symmetry and suppressed outputs", "Subsection",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell["\<\
A Fourier multiport realizes the discrete Fourier transform. With one photon \
per input, Fourier symmetry makes certain transition amplitudes vanish. Exact \
matrix entries let us identify these suppressed occupation patterns without \
numerical tolerances.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build the three-mode Fourier multiport, called a tritter, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["FourierMatrix",
   BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
   ButtonData->{
     URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/FourierMatrix.html"], 
     None}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tritter", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],

Cell["Draw the tritter:", "Text",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tritter", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the exact output distribution for one photon per input:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tritter", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 " and the three fully bunched outcomes have nonzero probability. All \
permutations of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " are suppressed. Build the four-mode Fourier multiport:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fourier4", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],

Cell["Draw the four-mode network:", "Text",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fourier4", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell["Compute its output distribution for one photon per input:", "Text",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fourierProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"fourier4", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell["Count the suppressed occupation patterns:", "Text",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Count", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Values", "[", "fourierProbabilities", "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],

Cell["\<\
Count all occupation patterns with four photons in four modes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Length", "[", "fourierProbabilities", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:= ",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell["\<\
Fourier symmetry suppresses 25 of the 35 patterns. These exact zeros expose \
interference that is harder to analyze in a generic network.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reference:", "TI"],
 " M. C. Tichy, K. Mayer, A. Buchleitner, K. M\[OSlash]lmer, Phys. Rev. Lett. \
",
 StyleBox["113",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 020502 (2014)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell["\<\
4. Squeezed light: pair creation and Gaussian photon statistics\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell["\<\
Squeezing makes a network active: energy exchange with a pump allows \
photon-pair creation and annihilation. Opposite single-mode squeezers \
followed by a balanced beam splitter prepare a two-mode squeezed vacuum. The \
two output modes have equal photon numbers.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build this preparation with a symbolic squeezing parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData["r"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"symbolicPair", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", "r", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"-", "r"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell["Draw the squeezed-vacuum preparation:", "Text",
 CellID->2099805207,ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"symbolicPair", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the probabilities of zero, one, and two pairs for positive ",
 Cell[BoxData["r"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"pairLawValues", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"symbolicPair", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    
    RowBox[{"r", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:= ",
 CellID->210724908,ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pair-number distribution is geometric: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["tanh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cosh",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 ". Verify the first three probabilities:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1992790374,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"pairLawValues", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Tanh", "[", "r", "]"}], "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], ")"}]}], "/", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Cosh", "[", "r", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"r", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[39]:= ",
 CellID->292747604,ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the infinite pair-number distribution is normalized:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1553818268,ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Tanh", "[", "r", "]"}], "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], ")"}]}], "/", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Cosh", "[", "r", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "Infinity"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "1"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[40]:= ",
 CellID->1870754514,ExpressionUUID->"0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],

Cell["Check that zero squeezing gives vacuum:", "Text",
 CellID->1358728755,ExpressionUUID->"7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
   RowBox[{"pairLawValues", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[41]:= ",
 CellID->935019337,ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Set the squeezing parameter to ",
 Cell[BoxData["0.5"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " for a numerical comparison:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->642744358,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tmsv", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", "0.5", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"-", "0.5"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[42]:= ",
 CellID->1478372881,ExpressionUUID->"2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],

Cell["Draw this squeezed-vacuum preparation:", "Text",
 CellID->124263719,ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tmsv", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[43]:= ",
 CellID->1310926461,ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "List probabilities through six total photons, omitting numerical residuals \
below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1124211690,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"tmsv", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Cutoff\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "6"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"#", " ", ">", " ", 
     RowBox[{"10", "^", 
      RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[44]:= ",
 CellID->1335749844,ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Only patterns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 " occur. Either mode alone has a thermal photon-number distribution. Compute \
the geometric probabilities for the retained pair numbers:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->793802945,ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Tanh", "[", "0.5", "]"}], "^", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], ")"}]}], "/", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cosh", "[", "0.5", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[45]:= ",
 CellID->631769182,ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell["\<\
For a four-mode example, prepare one squeezed vacuum in each mode:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1873681340,ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"squeezers", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", "0.6", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", "4", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[46]:= ",
 CellID->1468251080,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell["Draw the four squeezers:", "Text",
 CellID->1989234463,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"squeezers", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[47]:= ",
 CellID->1607696641,ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell["Set the random seed for the passive network:", "Text",
 CellID->1817342824,ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[48]:= ",
 CellID->530774412,ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],

Cell["Build a random four-mode passive network:", "Text",
 CellID->599957810,ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"randomMixer", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Random\>\"", "[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[49]:= ",
 CellID->1899946997,ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell["Draw the passive network:", "Text",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"randomMixer", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[50]:= ",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell["Apply the passive network after the squeezers:", "Text",
 CellID->1207491739,ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gbs", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"randomMixer", "[", "squeezers", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[51]:= ",
 CellID->216741342,ExpressionUUID->"0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],

Cell["Draw the combined network:", "Text",
 CellID->2096934290,ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gbs", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[52]:= ",
 CellID->1367217003,ExpressionUUID->"1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The vacuum-to-four-photon amplitude is a normalized hafnian. Such \
amplitudes determine the probabilities in Gaussian boson sampling. Compute \
the amplitude for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1372538143,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gaussianAmplitude", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gbs", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", 
     "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[53]:= ",
 CellID->485911656,ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell["Build the Fock-space circuit with six levels per mode:", "Text",
 CellID->181917407,ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gaussianFockCircuit", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gbs", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<CircuitOperator\>\"", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[54]:= ",
 CellID->1906087345,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell["Apply the circuit to vacuum:", "Text",
 CellID->354048744,ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gaussianFockOutput", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gaussianFockCircuit", "[", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[55]:= ",
 CellID->786710823,ExpressionUUID->"6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],

Cell["Compute the overlap with the four-photon target:", "Text",
 CellID->1859374462,ExpressionUUID->"25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fockAmplitude", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SuperDagger", "[", 
      RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",",
         " ", "6"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "@", " ", "gaussianFockOutput"}], 
    ")"}], "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[56]:= ",
 CellID->544914423,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],

Cell["Compare the two amplitudes:", "Text",
 CellID->1088734259,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
  RowBox[{"gaussianAmplitude", " ", "-", " ", "fockAmplitude"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[57]:= ",
 CellID->476175344,ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell["\<\
The difference is at machine precision. The hafnian calculation avoids \
constructing the full Fock-space circuit.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->201272189,ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["References:", "TI"],
 " C. S. Hamilton et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. ",
 StyleBox["119",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", 170501 (2017); hafnian algorithm, A. Bj\[ODoubleDot]rklund, B. Gupt, N. \
Quesada, arXiv:1805.12498."
}], "Text",
 CellID->320292756,ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell["\<\
5. Mach-Zehnder interferometry: controlling the output with a phase\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1146801282,ExpressionUUID->"7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two balanced beam splitters and an internal phase shift form a Mach-Zehnder \
interferometer. The phase controls the single-photon output probabilities. \
Build it with symbolic phase ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Phi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->41202278,ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mz", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<PS\>\"", "[", "\[Phi]", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[58]:= ",
 CellID->1124146653,ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell["Draw the Mach-Zehnder interferometer:", "Text",
 CellID->1232284935,ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mz", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[59]:= ",
 CellID->2082395230,ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the output amplitudes for a photon in the first input:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2045146513,ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mz", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[60]:= ",
 CellID->25123057,ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first-output probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],
 ". Compute it for a real phase:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->371825621,ExpressionUUID->"20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mz", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[61]:= ",
 CellID->1439628390,ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second-output probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],
 ". Compute it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->497245720,ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mz", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[62]:= ",
 CellID->1090726268,ExpressionUUID->"201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Set the phase to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1.0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 " for a Fock-space comparison:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2124519200,ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mz1", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<PS\>\"", "[", "1.0", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[63]:= ",
 CellID->617350884,ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell["Draw the interferometer with this phase:", "Text",
 CellID->1357963930,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mz1", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[64]:= ",
 CellID->1626918454,ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],

Cell["Compute the two-photon output distribution using permanents:", "Text",
 CellID->675379980,ExpressionUUID->"3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mzProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mz1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[65]:= ",
 CellID->1331866192,ExpressionUUID->"0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],

Cell["Build the Fock-space circuit with three levels per mode:", "Text",
 CellID->1391655620,ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mzFockCircuit", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mz1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<CircuitOperator\>\"", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[66]:= ",
 CellID->861714746,ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell["Propagate one photon in each input mode:", "Text",
 CellID->1192942815,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mzFockOutput", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mzFockCircuit", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[67]:= ",
 CellID->556077107,ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell["Read the output probabilities:", "Text",
 CellID->15883883,ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fockProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mzFockOutput", "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[68]:= ",
 CellID->308842859,ExpressionUUID->"0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],

Cell["\<\
Subtract the distributions by matching their occupation patterns:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1108042358,ExpressionUUID->"0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mzProbabilityDifferences", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Merge", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"mzProbabilities", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "fockProbabilities"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Total"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[69]:= ",
 CellID->1009200201,ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell["Compute the largest absolute probability difference:", "Text",
 CellID->752465254,ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Values", "[", "mzProbabilityDifferences", "]"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[70]:= ",
 CellID->891183881,ExpressionUUID->"128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],

Cell["\<\
The distributions agree to machine precision. Construct the inverse \
interferometer:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->741634648,ExpressionUUID->"3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"inverseMZ", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mz", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[71]:= ",
 CellID->359589406,ExpressionUUID->"50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],

Cell["\<\
Draw the inverse, which reverses the element order and inverts each element:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->533832725,ExpressionUUID->"640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"inverseMZ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[72]:= ",
 CellID->739917449,ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell["Apply the inverse after the original interferometer:", "Text",
 CellID->473762610,ExpressionUUID->"387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"roundTripMZ", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"inverseMZ", "[", "mz", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[73]:= ",
 CellID->1751712322,ExpressionUUID->"3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],

Cell["Draw the complete sequence:", "Text",
 CellID->1390140890,ExpressionUUID->"399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"roundTripMZ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[74]:= ",
 CellID->1031105928,ExpressionUUID->"1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],

Cell["Verify that the combined transfer matrix is the identity:", "Text",
 CellID->1410588720,ExpressionUUID->"6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"roundTripMZ", "[", "\"\<Unitary\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[75]:= ",
 CellID->1051974278,ExpressionUUID->"54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],

Cell["Part II: Input states and multiphoton interference", "Section",
 CellID->1989924844,ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell["\<\
Changing the input state changes the interference and photon statistics, even \
in the same network.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->695529426,ExpressionUUID->"74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],

Cell["6. Coherent inputs: photon statistics and dark ports", "Subsection",
 CellID->767788723,ExpressionUUID->"735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A coherent state with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 " and a one-photon Fock state both have mean photon number one. The coherent \
state's photon number fluctuates; the Fock state's does not."
}], "Text",
 CellID->494419947,ExpressionUUID->"3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a1", ",", " ", "a2"}], "}"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],
 " specifies coherent amplitudes. Their squared moduli sum to the mean total \
photon number, so this vector need not have unit norm. A plain list specifies \
a Fock-state occupation pattern instead."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1581507689,ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the output coherent amplitudes for input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2120100675,ExpressionUUID->"794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[76]:= ",
 CellID->950326543,ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compare the output distribution for the one-photon Fock input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1689126594,ExpressionUUID->"27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[77]:= ",
 CellID->1490757098,ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell["\<\
The coherent input can produce vacuum. Verify its vacuum probability:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->148290444,ExpressionUUID->"57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[78]:= ",
 CellID->1707667820,ExpressionUUID->"0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the three output probabilities with exactly two photons:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->933399197,ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"coherentTwoPhotonProbabilities", " ", "=", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}],
       "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[79]:= ",
 CellID->955179929,ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell["Add them to obtain the total two-photon probability:", "Text",
 CellID->775067320,ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twoPhotonProbability", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Total", "[", "coherentTwoPhotonProbabilities", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[80]:= ",
 CellID->72268088,ExpressionUUID->"499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],

Cell["\<\
Verify the two-photon probability for a Poisson distribution with mean one:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->546416532,ExpressionUUID->"0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twoPhotonProbability", " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "]"}], "/", "2"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[81]:= ",
 CellID->2117784656,ExpressionUUID->"0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],

Cell["\<\
Photon-number conservation forbids vacuum from the one-photon Fock input. \
Check it:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->853117843,ExpressionUUID->"6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[82]:= ",
 CellID->623836386,ExpressionUUID->"2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],

Cell["It also forbids a two-photon output. Check one such outcome:", "Text",
 CellID->564394165,ExpressionUUID->"06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[83]:= ",
 CellID->2048244887,ExpressionUUID->"25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],

Cell["\<\
A coherent-state distribution has an infinite tail. A finite cutoff omits \
probability; it does not justify renormalization. List the probabilities \
through six total photons:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1432457359,ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"coherentProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Cutoff\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "6"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[84]:= ",
 CellID->200346680,ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the retained probability equals the Poisson cumulative \
probability:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->447384324,ExpressionUUID->"7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Total", "[", "coherentProbabilities", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"CDF", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PoissonDistribution", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", "6"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[85]:= ",
 CellID->1438124241,ExpressionUUID->"3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Equal coherent amplitudes interfere destructively in one output, making it \
a ",
 StyleBox["dark port",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". Compute the output coherent amplitudes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2000382747,ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[86]:= ",
 CellID->902867877,ExpressionUUID->"473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],

Cell["Verify that the dark port cannot contain a photon:", "Text",
 CellID->1315202099,ExpressionUUID->"12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[87]:= ",
 CellID->376763343,ExpressionUUID->"1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Fock input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 " instead bunches into either output. Compute the probability that both \
photons leave through the port that was dark for the coherent input:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->126027414,ExpressionUUID->"43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[88]:= ",
 CellID->570920987,ExpressionUUID->"5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Coherent-state interference depends on the relative input phase. Give both \
inputs coherent amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Alpha]Laser"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],
 " and add phase ",
 Cell[BoxData["laserPhase"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],
 " to the second. Compute the output amplitudes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->378517449,ExpressionUUID->"5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"coherentOutput", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]Laser", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]Laser", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", "laserPhase"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[89]:= ",
 CellID->1671903560,ExpressionUUID->"7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["First"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],
 " extracts the coherent amplitude vector from the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Coherent\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],
 " expression. Its squared moduli are the mean output photon numbers, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "{", "1", "-", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],
 ", for relative phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],
 ". Verify this law:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1307059254,ExpressionUUID->"14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"First", "[", "coherentOutput", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "==",
     "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Alpha]Laser", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "laserPhase", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "laserPhase", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"laserPhase", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[90]:= ",
 CellID->538512558,ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The total mean photon number stays fixed. Compare the output amplitudes at \
relative phases zero and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->824717693,ExpressionUUID->"06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{"coherentOutput", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"laserPhase", " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "\[Pi]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[91]:= ",
 CellID->496527141,ExpressionUUID->"05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],

Cell["\<\
Changing the relative phase exchanges the dark port while preserving the \
input mean photon number.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2009363188,ExpressionUUID->"583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Source:", "TI"],
 " Agarwal, ",
 StyleBox["Quantum Optics", "TI"],
 ", Sections 5.3-5.5, pp. 105-107; Gerry and Knight, ",
 StyleBox["Introductory Quantum Optics", "TI"],
 ", Section 6.2."
}], "Text",
 CellID->55669068,ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell["7. Twin Fock inputs: why odd photon numbers are suppressed", \
"Subsection",
 CellID->1753574084,ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell["\<\
A twin Fock input has equal photon numbers in the two modes. Start with three \
photons per input of the balanced beam splitter. Compute the output \
distribution:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2038359728,ExpressionUUID->"60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twinProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[92]:= ",
 CellID->1525364821,ExpressionUUID->"40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every odd output photon number is suppressed. To examine arbitrary inputs, \
use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"nTwin", ",", " ", "nTwin"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],
 " and the photon-number-conserving output ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"mTwin", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "nTwin"}], " ", "-", " ", "mTwin"}]}], "}"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],
 ". The physical domain is integer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "mTwin", " ", "<=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "nTwin"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1535108406,ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell["\<\
Store the symbolic transition amplitude with its occupation domain:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1528788962,ExpressionUUID->"73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"symbolicTwinAmplitude", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"balanced", "[", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"nTwin", ",", " ", "nTwin"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"mTwin", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "nTwin"}], " ", "-", " ", "mTwin"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[93]:= ",
 CellID->1505774531,ExpressionUUID->"69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Refine",
   BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
   ButtonData->{
     URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Refine.html"], None}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],
 " removes the domain conditions when the occupations are assumed physical. \
Display the amplitude on this domain:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->535490749,ExpressionUUID->"10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Refine", "[", 
  RowBox[{"symbolicTwinAmplitude", ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"nTwin", ",", " ", "mTwin"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Integers"}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "mTwin", " ", "<=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "nTwin"}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[94]:= ",
 CellID->1238905205,ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["WignerD",
   BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
   ButtonData->{
     URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/WignerD.html"], None}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],
 " rotation matrix element ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],
 " in Wolfram's convention. The stored expression still returns zero outside \
its nonnegative-integer domain. Check negative and fractional substitutions:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2125008310,ExpressionUUID->"763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"symbolicTwinAmplitude", " ", "/.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", "->", " ", "#"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"mTwin", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[95]:= ",
 CellID->1684656716,ExpressionUUID->"635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],

Cell["\<\
Substitute three photons per input and order the amplitudes by the first \
output's photon number:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2057792111,ExpressionUUID->"0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twinSymbolicSix", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"symbolicTwinAmplitude", " ", "/.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", "->", " ", "3"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"mTwin", " ", "->", " ", "q"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"q", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[96]:= ",
 CellID->408837332,ExpressionUUID->"5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],

Cell["\<\
The amplitudes retain relative signs. Verify that their squared moduli give \
the direct QI probabilities:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1068510841,ExpressionUUID->"182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "twinSymbolicSix", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"q", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"6", " ", "-", " ", "q"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"q", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[97]:= ",
 CellID->1027032549,ExpressionUUID->"3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The general odd-output ",
 Cell[BoxData["WignerD"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],
 " expression does not simplify automatically in this kernel. A \
creation-operator argument gives the parity rule directly."
}], "Text",
 CellID->171792661,ExpressionUUID->"6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],
 " represent the output creation operators. One input pair contributes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "1"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2", "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2", "2"], "-", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "1", "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],
 ". Apart from input Fock normalization, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],
 " pairs therefore give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2", "2"], "-", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["z", "TI"], "1", "2"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],
 ". Only even powers occur, so neither output can have an odd photon number."
}], "Text",
 CellID->574949478,ExpressionUUID->"4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],

Cell["Expand the six-photon polynomial:", "Text",
 CellID->1664775781,ExpressionUUID->"67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Expand", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"z2", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"z1", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "^", "3"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"2", "^", "3"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[98]:= ",
 CellID->884697794,ExpressionUUID->"16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],

Cell["Verify the odd-output suppression in the QI distribution:", "Text",
 CellID->784201795,ExpressionUUID->"70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"KeySelect", "[", 
    RowBox[{"twinProbabilities", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"OddQ", "[", 
       RowBox[{"First", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<Name\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], 
    "]"}], ",", " ", "PossibleZeroQ"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[99]:= ",
 CellID->1193259712,ExpressionUUID->"7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"],

Cell["Verify normalization of the complete distribution:", "Text",
 CellID->1084903799,ExpressionUUID->"5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Total", "[", "twinProbabilities", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "1"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[100]:= ",
 CellID->964492758,ExpressionUUID->"013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],
 ", the coefficient of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "1", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "2", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "2", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
     "Binomial"], "/", 
    SuperscriptBox["2", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],
 ". Multiplying by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"2", 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"2", 
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "2", 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "!"}]], "/", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],
 " gives the normalized Fock-state amplitude. Its squared modulus is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
    "Binomial"], 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", 
        StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], 
        StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}], 
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]},
     "Binomial"], "/", 
    SuperscriptBox["4", 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->242210635,ExpressionUUID->"4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],

Cell["\<\
Form the normalized amplitude for the even-output occupation pattern:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->360816480,ExpressionUUID->"5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"twinEvenAmplitude", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ")"}], "^", "kTwin"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
     RowBox[{"nTwin", ",", " ", "kTwin"}], "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\n", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "kTwin"}], ")"}], "!"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "nTwin"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "kTwin"}]}], ")"}], "!"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", "^", "nTwin"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"nTwin", "!"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[101]:= ",
 CellID->1505759259,ExpressionUUID->"12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],

Cell["Compute its probability on the physical integer domain:", "Text",
 CellID->1384053022,ExpressionUUID->"451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"twinEvenProbability", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "twinEvenAmplitude", "]"}], "^", "2"}], ",", "\n", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"nTwin", ",", " ", "kTwin"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Integers"}], 
       "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "kTwin", " ", "<=", " ", "nTwin"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[102]:= ",
 CellID->1395659232,ExpressionUUID->"13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"],

Cell["Verify the binomial form of this probability:", "Text",
 CellID->874592789,ExpressionUUID->"445bf28f-7a5a-ecd1-6c78-ebe97fecb63b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"twinEvenProbability", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "kTwin"}], ",", " ", "kTwin"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", "-", " ", "kTwin"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", "-", " ", "kTwin"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"4", "^", "nTwin"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"nTwin", ",", " ", "kTwin"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Integers"}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "kTwin", " ", "<=", " ", "nTwin"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[103]:= ",
 CellID->1596157938,ExpressionUUID->"089aa42d-ce49-3603-38b9-3e76ebfd9d69"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify normalization for every nonnegative integer input using ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Sum",
   BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
   ButtonData->{
     URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Sum.html"], None}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"48fccab3-b886-a0f7-7883-e3fd3930f2dd"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1496122589,ExpressionUUID->"0cdaad60-2181-5e26-34f9-454a5034250c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "kTwin"}], ",", " ", "kTwin"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", "-", " ", "kTwin"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", "-", " ", "kTwin"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"4", "^", "nTwin"}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"kTwin", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "nTwin"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{"nTwin", ",", " ", "Integers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "1"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[104]:= ",
 CellID->1956327387,ExpressionUUID->"542cff75-84e0-b601-7dd3-f73f2c9a1d6b"],

Cell["Define the even-output probability on its physical domain:", "Text",
 CellID->1131177628,ExpressionUUID->"00dd9d4d-f7ec-565f-30e2-151681993ca5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"twinLaw", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n_Integer", "?", "NonNegative"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"k_Integer", "?", "NonNegative"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/;", " ", 
   RowBox[{"k", " ", "<=", " ", "n"}]}], " ", ":=", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}], " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"n", " ", "-", " ", "k"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "-", " ", "k"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"4", "^", "n"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[105]:= ",
 CellID->611195905,ExpressionUUID->"0d66b502-775d-ec4c-3b1d-2d6c02e9b696"],

Cell["Check this law against the six-photon QI probabilities:", "Text",
 CellID->1202919897,ExpressionUUID->"3a3bfee8-9a0e-4a4b-6bd8-f7b21fbb1891"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"6", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"twinLaw", "[", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[106]:= ",
 CellID->1334651244,ExpressionUUID->"333832e2-8bec-4128-62c7-abcc2d991072"],

Cell["\<\
Check the symbolic QI amplitude against the law for zero through five photons \
per input:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->185339758,ExpressionUUID->"78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"symbolicTwinAmplitude", " ", "/.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"nTwin", " ", "->", " ", "n"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"mTwin", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "==", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"twinLaw", "[", 
     RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[107]:= ",
 CellID->1677030473,ExpressionUUID->"1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],

Cell["\<\
Check normalization independently using the complete QI distributions over \
this range:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->134345938,ExpressionUUID->"710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    "1"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[108]:= ",
 CellID->350820043,ExpressionUUID->"71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],

Cell["The range includes vacuum and the original two-photon case.", "Text",
 CellID->456450236,ExpressionUUID->"06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Source:", "TI"],
 " Agarwal, Section 5.7, p. 109. The accompanying errata corrects the paths \
in Figure 5.5."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1767337052,ExpressionUUID->"0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"],

Cell["\<\
8. Four-photon interference: tuning suppression with reflectivity\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1422053341,ExpressionUUID->"2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At a balanced beam splitter, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],
 " cannot produce ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],
 ". Verify this suppression:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->603286833,ExpressionUUID->"66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[109]:= ",
 CellID->1349832744,ExpressionUUID->"3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"],
 ", suppressing the same output requires a different reflectivity. Build a \
beam splitter with symbolic angle:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->16034565,ExpressionUUID->"12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fourBS", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[110]:= ",
 CellID->344152329,ExpressionUUID->"3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],

Cell["Draw the beam splitter:", "Text",
 CellID->622383932,ExpressionUUID->"64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fourBS", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[111]:= ",
 CellID->2102744249,ExpressionUUID->"7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the return amplitude for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->565659401,ExpressionUUID->"330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fourAmplitude", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"fourBS", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[112]:= ",
 CellID->561487989,ExpressionUUID->"38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],

Cell["\<\
Verify its expression in terms of transmission and reflection amplitudes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2021628840,ExpressionUUID->"70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fourAmplitude", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"6", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[113]:= ",
 CellID->41425461,ExpressionUUID->"737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Writing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],
 " gives return amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "-", "6", 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["R", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"],
 ". Find the physical reflectivities at which it vanishes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208764476,ExpressionUUID->"25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"suppressionSettings", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"reflectivity", " ", "/.", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"6", " ", "reflectivity", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "reflectivity"}], ")"}]}]}], " ", "==", 
       " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "reflectivity", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}], ",",
      "\n", " ", "reflectivity", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[114]:= ",
 CellID->1584634344,ExpressionUUID->"3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"],

Cell["Build a beam splitter at each suppression setting:", "Text",
 CellID->35679398,ExpressionUUID->"67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"suppressionDevices", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"ArcSin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", 
    "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "suppressionSettings"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[115]:= ",
 CellID->1113372800,ExpressionUUID->"1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],

Cell["Draw both beam splitters:", "Text",
 CellID->969867355,ExpressionUUID->"221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"#", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], 
    " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "suppressionDevices"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[116]:= ",
 CellID->1210037699,ExpressionUUID->"3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],

Cell["Verify zero return probability at both settings:", "Text",
 CellID->1239892393,ExpressionUUID->"287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"RootReduce", "[", 
    RowBox[{"#", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
  " ", "/@", " ", "suppressionDevices"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[117]:= ",
 CellID->1498748757,ExpressionUUID->"2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],

Cell["\<\
The settings exchange transmissivity and reflectivity. At either endpoint, \
the return probability is one. Plot the return probability across the full \
angular range:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1701544389,ExpressionUUID->"440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"fourAmplitude", "^", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Beam splitter angle\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<P({2,2} to {2,2})\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Four-photon suppression at two unbalanced settings\>\""}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "480"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[118]:= ",
 CellID->1682415361,ExpressionUUID->"141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The zeros depend on the input photon number. Compute the return amplitude \
for symbolic twin Fock input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"nReturn", ",", " ", "nReturn"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1697357464,ExpressionUUID->"3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"returnAmplitudeFamily", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"fourBS", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"nReturn", ",", " ", "nReturn"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"nReturn", ",", " ", "nReturn"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{"nReturn", ",", " ", "Integers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nReturn", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[119]:= ",
 CellID->1540797058,ExpressionUUID->"321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluate the amplitude for one, two, and three photons per input:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->768596373,ExpressionUUID->"1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"returnAmplitudeFamily", " ", "/.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"nReturn", " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
    "&"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[120]:= ",
 CellID->1985169054,ExpressionUUID->"3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],

Cell["\<\
The different angular polynomials have different zeros. Verify the \
four-photon member:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->770675313,ExpressionUUID->"087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"returnAmplitudeFamily", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"nReturn", " ", "->", " ", "2"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    "fourAmplitude"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[121]:= ",
 CellID->846554368,ExpressionUUID->"7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Source:", "TI"],
 " Agarwal, Exercises 5.6 and 5.9, pp. 134-135."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1952818843,ExpressionUUID->"2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],

Cell["\<\
9. A photon and coherent light: preparing a state by heralding\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->599175116,ExpressionUUID->"13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Coherent inputs remain coherent under passive optics. Adding a Fock-state \
input allows nonclassical state preparation by ",
 StyleBox["heralding",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": a specified detection outcome in one mode selects a conditional state in \
the other."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1234886004,ExpressionUUID->"6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build a beam splitter for one photon in the first input and coherent \
amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Beta]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 " in the second:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1955603644,ExpressionUUID->"53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mixedBS", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[122]:= ",
 CellID->529524776,ExpressionUUID->"696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],

Cell["\<\
Draw the beam splitter; the first output will be measured for the heralding \
outcome:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->186212144,ExpressionUUID->"0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"mixedBS", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[123]:= ",
 CellID->284725946,ExpressionUUID->"640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Keep ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Beta]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],
 " complex. For one photon detected in the first output, compute the vacuum \
and one-photon amplitudes in the second:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1006536905,ExpressionUUID->"2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"heraldLeading", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"mixedBS", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", "\[Beta]", "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "->",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "k"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[124]:= ",
 CellID->207506748,ExpressionUUID->"07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],

Cell["Verify the two unnormalized conditional amplitudes:", "Text",
 CellID->1146295856,ExpressionUUID->"539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"heraldLeading", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Beta]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "/", "2"}], 
      "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Beta]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[125]:= ",
 CellID->438365529,ExpressionUUID->"1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coherent amplitude controls the relative magnitude and phase of these \
coefficients. Verify that a phase shift of ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Beta]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],
 " rotates only the one-photon coefficient:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->174000849,ExpressionUUID->"09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"heraldLeading", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Beta]", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Beta]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{"I", " ", "heraldDrivePhase"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ")"}], " ", "==",
     "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"heraldLeading", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", "heraldDrivePhase"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "heraldDrivePhase"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     "Reals"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[126]:= ",
 CellID->766726627,ExpressionUUID->"0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Small transmission and coherent amplitudes suppress higher photon numbers. \
Set the transmission amplitude to ",
 Cell["1/5", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1506609767,ExpressionUUID->"1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"heraldBS", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"ArcCos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "5"}], "]"}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[127]:= ",
 CellID->281363281,ExpressionUUID->"10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],

Cell["Draw the preparation network:", "Text",
 CellID->1615544595,ExpressionUUID->"41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"heraldBS", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[128]:= ",
 CellID->1805673747,ExpressionUUID->"62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Beta]", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "5"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],
 " and list joint probabilities through six total photons:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1547520620,ExpressionUUID->"166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mixedProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"heraldBS", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "5"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Cutoff\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "6"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[129]:= ",
 CellID->858350929,ExpressionUUID->"0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],

Cell["\<\
Select the joint outcomes with one photon in the first output:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2138894257,ExpressionUUID->"34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"N", "[", 
  RowBox[{"KeySelect", "[", 
   RowBox[{"mixedProbabilities", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"First", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<Name\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], 
     " ", "&"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[130]:= ",
 CellID->1941039383,ExpressionUUID->"15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],

Cell["\<\
These are joint probabilities before conditioning. To construct the \
conditional state, retain the corresponding amplitudes for zero through eight \
photons in the second output:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1670620029,ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"heraldAmplitudes", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"heraldBS", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
           RowBox[{"1", "/", "5"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "k"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[131]:= ",
 CellID->588214459,ExpressionUUID->"64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],

Cell["\<\
Their squared norm is the retained success probability. Compute it:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1759496502,ExpressionUUID->"67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"heraldSuccess", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "heraldAmplitudes", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[132]:= ",
 CellID->1641757231,ExpressionUUID->"233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],

Cell["Evaluate the retained success probability numerically:", "Text",
 CellID->896279625,ExpressionUUID->"7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"N", "[", "heraldSuccess", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[133]:= ",
 CellID->1264190945,ExpressionUUID->"4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],

Cell["\<\
Normalize the selected amplitudes to construct the conditional state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1806910998,ExpressionUUID->"598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"heraldState", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"heraldAmplitudes", "/", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "heraldSuccess", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "9"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[134]:= ",
 CellID->962064851,ExpressionUUID->"1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],

Cell["Verify normalization of the conditional state:", "Text",
 CellID->1660212291,ExpressionUUID->"7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"heraldState", "[", "\"\<Norm\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "1"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[135]:= ",
 CellID->1553450743,ExpressionUUID->"41ecc127-3c02-05fa-7793-d881b5b76fc0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The leading coefficients approximate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], "-", 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1190ff72-a9fe-60f8-47af-f73fcf8b32c2"],
 ". Compute the fidelity (squared overlap) with this target state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->376345483,ExpressionUUID->"19c80315-d7de-7125-4ff7-9b5ee26b400f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"N", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}], " ", ".", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
          RowBox[{"heraldState", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",",
          " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[136]:= ",
 CellID->1917523023,ExpressionUUID->"6fdf78a7-59a9-97d9-15e5-7101585dfd23"],

Cell["\<\
The fidelity applies to the retained state. Bound the omitted joint \
probability using the coherent input's Poisson tail:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->225924774,ExpressionUUID->"7a87483f-bfa4-2eb6-2abd-62793a51749c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"N", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"CDF", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"PoissonDistribution", "[", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "25"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   "20"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[137]:= ",
 CellID->1508526016,ExpressionUUID->"09b26917-59e6-8729-3f41-81515f90ea73"],

Cell["\<\
Photon-number conservation gives this bound: with one herald photon, an \
omitted output requires more than eight photons from the coherent input. \
Divide by the retained success probability for an upper bound on the \
conditional tail.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1653333794,ExpressionUUID->"521ad179-838d-ce9b-0239-c923363994e1"],

Cell["\<\
At zero coherent amplitude, the heralding outcome leaves vacuum in the second \
output. Check its joint probability:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2117504204,ExpressionUUID->"136d7364-bcfb-8461-4113-6b4e348fef4b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"heraldBS", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", "0", "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "25"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[138]:= ",
 CellID->201091240,ExpressionUUID->"2b78534b-7a52-d624-5918-4b157fe4bd0e"],

Cell["Verify that no photon can remain in the second output:", "Text",
 CellID->667003370,ExpressionUUID->"30c454b2-bdb8-e427-60fc-4dfc3432cf0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"heraldBS", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", "0", "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[139]:= ",
 CellID->526043023,ExpressionUUID->"6879dfe8-0276-0c7b-1806-d6b2b7035741"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Source:", "TI"],
 " Agarwal, Section 5.9 and Figure 5.6, pp. 110-111. Relative signs follow \
our real beam splitter convention."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1120596176,ExpressionUUID->"7cc522fa-6a93-e579-24fa-bba40f27cc43"],

Cell["\<\
10. Multiphoton interferometry: fringes and factorial moments\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->64105026,ExpressionUUID->"5b82e386-6ff5-c0ee-09b1-fae009819234"],

Cell["\<\
A fringe is the phase dependence of a specified outcome for a specified \
input. Compute the single-photon return probability in the Mach-Zehnder \
interferometer:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1373525465,ExpressionUUID->"34a39a2f-b372-ffce-5c50-1388c604c514"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fringeOne", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"mz", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[140]:= ",
 CellID->1964307623,ExpressionUUID->"66ca9132-7812-8248-0ec9-097c79a4d092"],

Cell["Verify the single-photon fringe:", "Text",
 CellID->39040159,ExpressionUUID->"023b1c4a-5b09-a8c9-33d8-96145ebdfa13"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fringeOne", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Phi]", "/", "2"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[141]:= ",
 CellID->1242473813,ExpressionUUID->"29a4f364-fd74-7ca4-5f5b-eb41f401468e"],

Cell["Compute the coincidence fringe for one photon per input:", "Text",
 CellID->290269587,ExpressionUUID->"47740231-7fc8-4299-6d0b-a47b7a7d10e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fringeTwo", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"mz", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[142]:= ",
 CellID->471335900,ExpressionUUID->"1af52337-5e42-c8c3-4a8a-bb715bf49a29"],

Cell["Verify the two-photon fringe:", "Text",
 CellID->1843091513,ExpressionUUID->"2fdb82dc-2353-e9b3-55f8-1b8656e7bb99"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fringeTwo", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Phi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[143]:= ",
 CellID->1978684664,ExpressionUUID->"5782d92f-a790-094a-7db1-d088d2255b90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the probability of output ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05d48452-325d-a277-33eb-1e1c47e9f15d"],
 " for input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087ffcf6-194e-431e-3804-f5b098fb2e64"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2064137570,ExpressionUUID->"615fadf7-df9a-5675-1764-44b0da2f3d5f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fringeFour", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"mz", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[144]:= ",
 CellID->1265784226,ExpressionUUID->"5de452e3-5fd7-a751-0b9c-4bcd5a630dbb"],

Cell["Verify the four-photon fringe:", "Text",
 CellID->872599864,ExpressionUUID->"2d0df906-1ebb-1081-5b32-f1609b4e62eb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fringeFour", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"3", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", "8"}]}]}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Phi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[145]:= ",
 CellID->2056057710,ExpressionUUID->"519a4e0d-3467-bfb9-07ba-6057bd130583"],

Cell["\<\
The four-photon fringe has a shorter period and a lower detection \
probability. A shorter period alone does not establish better phase \
sensitivity; fluctuations and photon resources also matter. Plot the \
probabilities without rescaling:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1360523735,ExpressionUUID->"3a891815-8c00-cf41-6ab6-925f25ba95ab"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"fringeOne", ",", " ", "fringeTwo", ",", " ", "fringeFour"}], 
     "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Phi]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Internal phase\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<Outcome probability\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<{1,0} to {1,0}\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<{1,1} to {1,1}\>\"", ",",
       " ", "\"\<{2,2} to {3,1}\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Multiphoton outcome probabilities\>\""}],
    ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[146]:= ",
 CellID->676766013,ExpressionUUID->"0dbacffa-31b0-43f6-3b59-e6a4404511dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a three-photon example, use reflectivity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "/", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "196a859c-b643-c1b3-4f69-1cd9c3f79399"],
 " at both beam splitters, the symmetric reflection-phase convention, and \
phase factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[CurlyPhi]"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c8a383-1e42-ef31-78f7-3aed9bf4b21b"],
 " in the second arm. Build the interferometer:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1428640414,ExpressionUUID->"50735439-04fd-dee7-0001-4e63ac89a4cd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"threeMZ", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ArcSin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"2", "/", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<PS\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"-", "phase3"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
     
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ArcSin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"2", "/", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[147]:= ",
 CellID->1143649234,ExpressionUUID->"3597ba8d-914b-928f-63ac-33d720ffe0d5"],

Cell["Draw the three-photon interferometer:", "Text",
 CellID->1571962290,ExpressionUUID->"056fda38-a5bc-2884-3314-dc65cc497aee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"threeMZ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[148]:= ",
 CellID->2091585593,ExpressionUUID->"383c4a9f-130c-f8c1-69c4-63d9a6beca2b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the probability of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b649e79-a2e1-7610-291b-1022d6945d7a"],
 " becoming ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09cb884c-5fc8-b209-3fc8-22165a620153"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->30157833,ExpressionUUID->"376c6589-bcca-29e8-5d14-7cd3357f7b32"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"threeFringe", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"threeMZ", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"phase3", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[149]:= ",
 CellID->1715653387,ExpressionUUID->"667bb688-7420-22c7-0e18-2fd27dd5702d"],

Cell["Verify the fringe with three times the internal phase:", "Text",
 CellID->1904268993,ExpressionUUID->"72002252-da4c-5210-223f-c41fdff9217a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"threeFringe", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"16", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
         RowBox[{"3", " ", "phase3"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "81"}]}]}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"phase3", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[150]:= ",
 CellID->1610510011,ExpressionUUID->"084561a7-5440-aaee-387b-78015dfaf834"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The factorial moment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], "-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "721e71e5-9ca7-ded5-2226-68cf1553a43f"],
 " counts ordered detection triples. In this three-photon sector, only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a84e7eb-55e0-1894-3abb-feb563956afe"],
 " contributes, with factor two. Compute the complete output distribution:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1363210520,ExpressionUUID->"3261920b-7b77-02d6-621e-14557e02503c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"threeProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"threeMZ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[151]:= ",
 CellID->751311520,ExpressionUUID->"4ebe3b2c-9c8f-bd2d-7645-b376153b0477"],

Cell["Verify normalization before using the probabilities:", "Text",
 CellID->1811324800,ExpressionUUID->"7d6a0058-fb4a-caff-2b69-9a05fefc98c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", "threeProbabilities", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==",
   " ", "1"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[152]:= ",
 CellID->1255352889,ExpressionUUID->"41d92934-9aba-8299-77e6-c17e1f4cd0e3"],

Cell["Compute the factorial moment from the occupation patterns:", "Text",
 CellID->1056550259,ExpressionUUID->"5cc23ff5-bf0f-f019-04f1-b6bf3abbc363"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"factorialMoment", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<Name\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"#2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"n", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"n", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"n", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}]}], 
        "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "threeProbabilities"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[153]:= ",
 CellID->1554899303,ExpressionUUID->"29880975-91f0-008f-5fb7-a13f278552d5"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the moment is twice the selected outcome probability:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1285549060,ExpressionUUID->"551c00cf-fc58-99c4-0323-99a8f5d2eb2e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", "[", 
    RowBox[{"factorialMoment", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "threeFringe"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[154]:= ",
 CellID->1616846310,ExpressionUUID->"22235db8-54be-42b7-53d1-54e25d4b109d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Source:", "TI"],
 " Agarwal, Sections 5.12, 5.15-5.16, pp. 113-123, and Exercise 5.10."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1706199142,ExpressionUUID->"0976d5ae-737d-f257-3f0d-cc080609c0bd"],

Cell["Part III: State preparation, loss, and photonic computation", "Section",
 CellID->848974671,ExpressionUUID->"13e711b4-4d78-4d68-419c-88fe640d17b2"],

Cell["\<\
We now reverse a preparation, apply pure loss, and compose larger optical \
networks.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1375299215,ExpressionUUID->"3fd09d86-aea1-a602-65ef-14e3cb550d68"],

Cell["11. Squeezed-state interference: disentangling two modes", "Subsection",
 CellID->1656178105,ExpressionUUID->"2f6c0922-6605-ed68-5513-a08c13b1b7b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["symbolicPair"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2caab86a-2af9-b1b1-54a9-32344e8d039b"],
 " prepares a two-mode squeezed vacuum by mixing opposite single-mode \
squeezed vacua. Reversing its beam splitter should recover the independent \
squeezed vacua. Keep ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"r", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f56169e-4783-4dbb-256d-8fd872361781"],
 " symbolic and construct the inverse beam splitter:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2128368636,ExpressionUUID->"5b84d4d6-858d-5842-09bb-cd902c382aa8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"inverseBalanced", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"balanced", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[155]:= ",
 CellID->471452856,ExpressionUUID->"67558936-e5eb-8680-0d6a-2173939fecea"],

Cell["Draw the inverse beam splitter:", "Text",
 CellID->1993504316,ExpressionUUID->"1072dc7c-f7d5-c74e-4001-d6398261ad94"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"inverseBalanced", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[156]:= ",
 CellID->1944276818,ExpressionUUID->"3462f0a3-098c-f6b3-5c11-e90da83edc99"],

Cell["Apply it after the two-mode squeezed-vacuum preparation:", "Text",
 CellID->524220529,ExpressionUUID->"04cac1af-436c-9192-2cc9-d809761ee3f8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"separatedSqueezers", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"inverseBalanced", "[", "symbolicPair", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[157]:= ",
 CellID->950216136,ExpressionUUID->"63be94f2-239e-9b81-1145-0dbc5628e9eb"],

Cell["Draw the full sequence:", "Text",
 CellID->338647958,ExpressionUUID->"5a3d7a71-218e-1995-0bc3-7c3b503b6bff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"separatedSqueezers", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[158]:= ",
 CellID->961910044,ExpressionUUID->"3a0f2024-2f71-09ca-6a34-b98e4a045b10"],

Cell["\<\
Build the direct preparation with the same squeezing parameter:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1465513701,ExpressionUUID->"277956ac-4c9d-d338-4d07-4ff66529be02"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"directSqueezers", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", "r", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"-", "r"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}]}], "}"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[159]:= ",
 CellID->1779278278,ExpressionUUID->"178a6a52-23e4-1142-3d89-8c1c559163a8"],

Cell["Draw the direct preparation:", "Text",
 CellID->332869652,ExpressionUUID->"52ddf811-e480-8137-02e2-f25a8d3ad01d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"directSqueezers", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[160]:= ",
 CellID->870462011,ExpressionUUID->"719ae17a-c654-ed44-27b9-f927f3e6b7ae"],

Cell["Choose output occupations zero through six in each mode:", "Text",
 CellID->770594293,ExpressionUUID->"62c8f42b-c628-388a-12f7-ee74f3c28ad0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"squeezePatterns", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[161]:= ",
 CellID->416617480,ExpressionUUID->"36e5ffeb-8179-694d-5e9a-f6b5300c3b97"],

Cell["\<\
Subtract the preparation amplitudes for each occupation pattern:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->468951994,ExpressionUUID->"7af061c8-c44a-ae8e-2a80-7895edfcf4d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"squeezeAmplitudeDifferences", " ", "=", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"separatedSqueezers", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], 
        "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"directSqueezers", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "squeezePatterns"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[162]:= ",
 CellID->1802328397,ExpressionUUID->"0d437dad-8290-de9a-3b71-74f7372aa4e0"],

Cell["Find the largest absolute difference for positive squeezing:", "Text",
 CellID->328865975,ExpressionUUID->"7aafc905-908a-67da-2a54-e16f213f4d20"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"separationError", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "squeezeAmplitudeDifferences", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[163]:= ",
 CellID->1270006433,ExpressionUUID->"62016b94-8ad8-fb56-123e-82de2f52c9bc"],

Cell["Verify exact agreement for positive squeezing:", "Text",
 CellID->34003199,ExpressionUUID->"0e7c794a-82c2-56e7-3604-711437773ccd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"separationError", " ", "==", " ", "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[164]:= ",
 CellID->1596250240,ExpressionUUID->"30f601cf-5001-fb68-608d-98a961b5c9b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The independent squeezed vacua have factorized probabilities. Each has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
     "Binomial"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["tanh",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "/", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["4", 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["cosh",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04bc0f0b-f02f-243d-2c43-a75481db8f07"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a24bdc2-598a-1b95-4bdb-34ac583f69ff"],
 ". Define this single-mode probability, including the vacuum case:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1572158672,ExpressionUUID->"705e212e-f5a4-7717-2065-b88bfc515a7d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"singleSqueezedProbability", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"n_Integer", "?", "NonNegative"}], ",", " ", "r_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=",
   "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"If", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"EvenQ", "[", "n", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"If", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"n", " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Tanh", "[", "r", "]"}], "^", "n"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", "^", "n"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"Cosh", "[", "r", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[165]:= ",
 CellID->1137775047,ExpressionUUID->"5c2f5325-a3f6-c048-05d5-4a8ed5809292"],

Cell["Verify the zero-squeezing vacuum probability:", "Text",
 CellID->573363004,ExpressionUUID->"211ecaf2-61ee-418f-5725-e3bc179b13d5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"singleSqueezedProbability", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[166]:= ",
 CellID->1565937439,ExpressionUUID->"51e4dffc-d38f-5703-079b-d6b9e63a3a69"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the single-mode probabilities for zero through four photons:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1825661031,ExpressionUUID->"30e43b5d-74af-d0fb-609b-b3077d5ba2c1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"singleSqueezedValues", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"singleSqueezedProbability", "[", 
      RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[167]:= ",
 CellID->1952919625,ExpressionUUID->"44d9380c-2e05-8f35-6ce6-b2564bb1d21f"],

Cell["\<\
Independent modes have joint probabilities given by an outer product. Form \
that reference matrix:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->162062935,ExpressionUUID->"36758762-649a-f7b1-5e0a-1f4c0d2cdd9b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"independentSqueezedProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "Times", ",", " ", "singleSqueezedValues", ",", " ", 
     "singleSqueezedValues"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[168]:= ",
 CellID->1483832353,ExpressionUUID->"138e1639-4d05-8b97-41b5-886364b1d9fd"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the joint probabilities after separation, with rows for mode 1 and \
columns for mode 2:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->421271511,ExpressionUUID->"156728ce-0023-e03b-431c-c1a8b1d7b301"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"separatedSqueezedProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"separatedSqueezers", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "k"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[169]:= ",
 CellID->971430162,ExpressionUUID->"7fc37353-2ed8-42c8-25f1-6b1d4b6d1012"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify factorization for arbitrary positive ",
 Cell[BoxData["r"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26ff5c08-e081-ff27-4e85-56559135c20d"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->411794565,ExpressionUUID->"07c988c4-3ef2-8066-2df6-21aeba84d34c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
   "separatedSqueezedProbabilities", " ", "==", " ", 
    "independentSqueezedProbabilities"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"r", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[170]:= ",
 CellID->211393631,ExpressionUUID->"4bc0a2f3-6150-447f-79ff-3bbd10e52f45"],

Cell["Gaussian decompositions: equivalent optical networks", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->485898233,ExpressionUUID->"7ac66077-3bfa-1f18-2afe-7a31bd8f6262"],

Cell["\<\
Bloch-Messiah decomposition writes a lossless Gaussian unitary as passive \
optics, single-mode squeezers, then passive optics. QI computes it for \
numerical optical parameters. Build a network with mode mixing before and \
after squeezing:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->300459616,ExpressionUUID->"3d863d84-94ab-5643-6bbd-b4ee1d5e3ca9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gaussianSequence", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", "0.3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", "0.5", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0.2", " ", "I"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.7", ",", " ", "0.4"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[171]:= ",
 CellID->1400905077,ExpressionUUID->"7ab8b877-e011-189c-2a47-323091a46ae6"],

Cell["Draw this network:", "Text",
 CellID->900992407,ExpressionUUID->"35eb0178-2238-e094-63e8-992257b2b2fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gaussianSequence", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[172]:= ",
 CellID->1909490419,ExpressionUUID->"0da6433d-a7a4-ba24-3b5e-5b66d256090e"],

Cell["Compute its Bloch-Messiah form:", "Text",
 CellID->809304935,ExpressionUUID->"462f64f6-435d-c7dd-6fd5-7db076e9ad27"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochMessiah", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gaussianSequence", "[", "\"\<BlochMessiah\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[173]:= ",
 CellID->1060035609,ExpressionUUID->"4b06bf63-5f43-ed7c-793d-374d5af7b446"],

Cell["Draw the decomposed network:", "Text",
 CellID->960351252,ExpressionUUID->"0fd1c247-21a4-d962-35ee-e4215056a848"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochMessiah", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[174]:= ",
 CellID->1269096941,ExpressionUUID->"09347675-9fce-c17b-38cc-683f1a789041"],

Cell["\<\
Equivalent forms can differ by a global phase, so compare probabilities. \
Choose zero through three photons per output mode:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2008479665,ExpressionUUID->"2c597ed5-00d9-d535-5467-779fb16dbc1f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"formPatterns", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[175]:= ",
 CellID->29625565,ExpressionUUID->"66c4d8d6-27c8-a0db-0efb-d1905262f221"],

Cell["Compare the two networks for a nonvacuum input:", "Text",
 CellID->9883570,ExpressionUUID->"4d3801b6-8b23-0df3-74c7-98f02ed657d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bmDifferences", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gaussianSequence", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], 
        "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"blochMessiah", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "formPatterns"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[176]:= ",
 CellID->940978275,ExpressionUUID->"09816d05-11e9-fb6e-3fbe-856fa79dc9b4"],

Cell["Verify agreement within numerical precision:", "Text",
 CellID->173258875,ExpressionUUID->"35ec423d-cde2-7917-6394-6466eb97487d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "bmDifferences", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[177]:= ",
 CellID->792860948,ExpressionUUID->"05e0e9bc-56b1-1bf2-339f-00e6634469d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For vacuum input, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<GBSForm\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46408f14-a324-388b-6e7f-2751d6d68ad1"],
 " moves all squeezers before a passive network. It preserves the output \
state for vacuum input, up to a global phase. Compute this form:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->124530881,ExpressionUUID->"40213c85-9219-7c2b-71de-b5ef27ac4771"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"vacuumForm", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gaussianSequence", "[", "\"\<GBSForm\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[178]:= ",
 CellID->1312473818,ExpressionUUID->"678faed4-2cca-f411-0db4-479e457cdf7b"],

Cell["Draw the squeezers followed by passive optics:", "Text",
 CellID->1627779716,ExpressionUUID->"3b3cac94-919f-f08d-6ac3-45de202bc2d7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"vacuumForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[179]:= ",
 CellID->294107029,ExpressionUUID->"634a1270-2707-566e-1149-943a52b23cb4"],

Cell["Compare the vacuum-input probabilities:", "Text",
 CellID->736271930,ExpressionUUID->"571f0194-b08e-3ab4-7d24-98d1c138889e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gbsDifferences", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gaussianSequence", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], 
        "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"vacuumForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "formPatterns"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[180]:= ",
 CellID->406066173,ExpressionUUID->"79764466-e076-5945-2f0e-5e4391032baf"],

Cell["Verify agreement within numerical precision:", "Text",
 CellID->783505316,ExpressionUUID->"54e8dec7-14b1-519a-7c97-d7a19d4423e0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "gbsDifferences", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[181]:= ",
 CellID->1838581182,ExpressionUUID->"25f5c72f-3423-741a-538a-de89bdd65f60"],

Cell["Photon-number cutoffs: retained and omitted probability", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellID->1015299810,ExpressionUUID->"6dbbd446-5835-e39a-1b58-ce2059c1b1e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The total photon-number cutoff differs from the number of Fock levels per \
mode. Return to ",
 Cell[BoxData["tmsv"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d34e655-b983-17e8-14cb-f81f38367d32"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"r", " ", "=", " ", "0.5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c435daa-0d1c-c5df-0471-54f4a4aeaf25"],
 ": cutoff ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21714cd0-c04e-e57a-570f-659df1f8cc40"],
 " retains pairs through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftFloor]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "/", "2"}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightFloor]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74ff421b-073b-c6d4-1c85-6445b2cfac3e"],
 ". Compute the retained probabilities at three cutoffs:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->320909480,ExpressionUUID->"3ebc3a74-dd7c-3fa6-6643-bc31d40e858c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"pairRetainedProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
      RowBox[{"tmsv", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Cutoff\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "#"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
     "&"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "8", ",", " ", "12"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[182]:= ",
 CellID->1950243504,ExpressionUUID->"7d5c93fe-a057-3a16-2b63-0abbd1e3897c"],

Cell["Compute the omitted probabilities:", "Text",
 CellID->1158471628,ExpressionUUID->"487dadd0-5ed6-7873-7802-449a5b634b59"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "#"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
   "pairRetainedProbabilities"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[183]:= ",
 CellID->600867794,ExpressionUUID->"5219761b-8a64-c9ff-0227-68452f169bc5"],

Cell["\<\
Verify the retained probabilities against the geometric tail formula:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->570648126,ExpressionUUID->"69346765-6d1c-e9c9-18cc-7f4f04aebb13"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"#2", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Tanh", "[", "0.5", "]"}], "^", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
               RowBox[{"#1", "/", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}],
            ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
     RowBox[{"10", "^", 
      RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   "pairRetainedProbabilities"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[184]:= ",
 CellID->1943045306,ExpressionUUID->"7c22b8c2-70f4-0562-25d1-31ac00816c48"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The retained probability approaches one without renormalizing the listed \
outcomes. QI computes squeezed-network probabilities directly. ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Samples\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04fec585-b88c-469b-2c85-dcef39392ce1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<SampleCounts\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aa617d4-4041-969d-2a5d-8e9e71f5fce7"],
 " support only lossless passive networks. Gaussian boson sampling here \
refers to the probability model."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1695469705,ExpressionUUID->"5e86e5c8-d785-1389-06bd-fc95e23061d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Source:", "TI"],
 " Agarwal, Section 5.8, p. 109, and Sections 3.1-3.2; Gerry and Knight, \
Section 7.7."
}], "Text",
 CellID->808446663,ExpressionUUID->"3582ea65-851b-2569-63b1-0c4f2caf8fb3"],

Cell["12. Pure loss: attenuation and mixed output states", "Subsection",
 CellID->843355028,ExpressionUUID->"5e81d752-d9a7-cf7a-06be-cf1fd8539240"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Loss\>\"", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6dc17641-57cc-3497-1bff-682b627e9efd"],
 " applies a pure-loss channel with ",
 StyleBox["transmissivity",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "647a9320-5a37-336f-0c19-0a8a5fc381b5"],
 ". A photon survives with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57b40e76-1aa6-da65-7d4b-a0309f50a94f"],
 "; the coherent amplitude scales by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "575b10e3-003a-b957-7d78-89cdb1cc0bbd"],
 ". The environment is in vacuum. QI computes the reduced output directly."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2123001010,ExpressionUUID->"7c7345dd-208f-a284-2401-5c87513bf0ee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build a one-mode attenuator, declaring ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Eta]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0121a537-2575-8479-30de-3d714c01ef43"],
 " for later substitution:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1415208481,ExpressionUUID->"7f325126-465a-e19d-26c2-488073ecb3e7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"attenuator", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Loss\>\"", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\[Eta]", "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[185]:= ",
 CellID->80082845,ExpressionUUID->"739af998-c5c1-31b3-21b9-f0c5ec758399"],

Cell["Draw the attenuator:", "Text",
 CellID->730828669,ExpressionUUID->"003becda-d908-4451-31d8-0587d8bd2ebb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"attenuator", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[186]:= ",
 CellID->20229285,ExpressionUUID->"7aeb468a-2cc6-59e2-2ae9-5fd445732bc8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<TransferMatrix\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3873a668-04d7-31ac-6800-3832ad6383f6"],
 " for a lossy device. Read the retained amplitude transformation:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->865532999,ExpressionUUID->"4156c81a-8a68-59d7-776d-e2442f1d2b3d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"attenuator", "[", "\"\<TransferMatrix\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[187]:= ",
 CellID->1719354248,ExpressionUUID->"569e7ab4-00f8-e339-7ea6-73feb172ce03"],

Cell["\<\
This matrix is generally nonunitary. Generic Fock transition amplitudes are \
unavailable for lossy devices because different environment outcomes \
contribute separate probabilities.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->803807756,ExpressionUUID->"0b3ec616-de69-0141-3ac5-d853db1c53ab"],

Cell["Fock inputs: binomial photon loss", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->601042471,ExpressionUUID->"7c0d57bf-7ae8-3253-2433-4ef97e8280b9"],

Cell["\<\
For three input photons, the retained photon number ranges from zero to \
three. Compute its distribution on the physical transmissivity domain:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2038927162,ExpressionUUID->"0aaecb0d-dff0-cd78-3a55-e356d98a9442"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Refine", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"attenuator", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "3", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[188]:= ",
 CellID->1188205371,ExpressionUUID->"4fe4a286-576e-fd11-759b-3be06218c47b"],

Cell["Verify normalization:", "Text",
 CellID->1003860385,ExpressionUUID->"07179650-9fbb-2bc1-2d2c-081a1a4e792b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", "lossProbabilities", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[189]:= ",
 CellID->952137231,ExpressionUUID->"7aecd320-e31f-2936-2a93-ca8d96aa781c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The entries are ordered by retained photon number. Verify the mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "326b0854-5043-0b63-6268-a21e61f65649"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1052272830,ExpressionUUID->"1d6edc53-4ce5-e0f2-4b15-d61d6491b2d8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Values", "[", "lossProbabilities", "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "\[Eta]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[190]:= ",
 CellID->775731387,ExpressionUUID->"45f7e4e6-4e1c-a184-738c-fdc06baef3ee"],

Cell["\<\
At unit transmissivity, all three photons survive. Check this limit:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->975612517,ExpressionUUID->"70e98525-204e-6ba4-2096-1c8f51fb398e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Values", "[", "lossProbabilities", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], 
   "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[191]:= ",
 CellID->105335494,ExpressionUUID->"704169dd-a4db-5005-207e-8086cd6e236f"],

Cell["\<\
At zero transmissivity, the output is vacuum. Check this limit:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1276006902,ExpressionUUID->"7b2d1c14-5aff-cd5f-2ad2-965e5e8b97a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Values", "[", "lossProbabilities", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], 
   "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[192]:= ",
 CellID->429330924,ExpressionUUID->"62ac11c1-6d0b-a8c0-1253-88ab04bffa2a"],

Cell["\<\
A Fock input generally becomes a mixture. Propagate three photons with four \
Fock levels:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->699653744,ExpressionUUID->"2e7621e1-2fba-a33a-560d-b8cb4a4c0e00"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"attenuatedState", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"attenuator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[193]:= ",
 CellID->2118070064,ExpressionUUID->"15938457-0322-a4d9-43a0-1e11b6d40e23"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the density matrix is diagonal with the calculated probabilities:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1744932242,ExpressionUUID->"7f1ed2e3-b722-4b37-2525-cbccc2d7161d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"attenuatedState", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
    " ", "==", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Values", "[", "lossProbabilities", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[194]:= ",
 CellID->551334296,ExpressionUUID->"52e63e44-9d5c-26a1-029d-b02e14ee8c8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Check the purity at transmissivity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e766a94-5ec6-6187-160d-83de5b7333ed"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->682025647,ExpressionUUID->"2eead67c-41e5-1519-56e9-c82677907c63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"attenuatedState", "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"5", "/", "16"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[195]:= ",
 CellID->1646424406,ExpressionUUID->"23a655ec-dad2-e192-515e-4cc9df64b3f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Independent attenuation also accepts symbolic photon numbers. Compute the \
probability that ",
 Cell[BoxData["nLoss"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62ef85cc-c62f-39ac-1294-1ca9f3db8bf6"],
 " input photons leave ",
 Cell[BoxData["kLoss"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d6c313b-6800-4a9b-2b13-a96509b518e1"],
 " survivors:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2053055694,ExpressionUUID->"75dfb56b-bb47-a02b-23e4-2d353ef3f371"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossCountLaw", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"attenuator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "nLoss", "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "kLoss", "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"nLoss", ",", " ", "kLoss"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Integers"}], 
       "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "kLoss", " ", "<=", " ", "nLoss"}], " ", "&&",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[196]:= ",
 CellID->2132198261,ExpressionUUID->"57533ce7-69d6-be0e-7d60-b5c108600554"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify the binomial law ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
     "Binomial"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"1", "-", 
       StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27c3fefb-2ee6-8038-4df0-f7a54a90d302"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1954495564,ExpressionUUID->"60d4995f-bb7f-b80c-10eb-11193e0b0b56"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"lossCountLaw", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
      RowBox[{"nLoss", ",", " ", "kLoss"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "^", "kLoss"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "\[Eta]"}], ")"}], "^", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"nLoss", " ", "-", " ", "kLoss"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"nLoss", ",", " ", "kLoss"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Integers"}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "kLoss", " ", "<=", " ", "nLoss"}], " ", "&&",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[197]:= ",
 CellID->1504758964,ExpressionUUID->"64608bbe-760c-8af3-0c1f-22f803bed8d9"],

Cell["\<\
Verify normalization for every nonnegative integer input photon number:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->885403737,ExpressionUUID->"09661063-a2cf-675e-3f1d-8a4cd77a4da4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
   RowBox[{"lossCountLaw", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"kLoss", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "nLoss"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{"nLoss", ",", " ", "Integers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"nLoss", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}]}]}], "]"}],
   " ", "==", " ", "1"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[198]:= ",
 CellID->299015440,ExpressionUUID->"5561d787-26b0-8d0a-031e-cee1534ad450"],

Cell["Compute the mean retained photon number:", "Text",
 CellID->59570862,ExpressionUUID->"0fea91e8-e80e-a1ed-35e9-08b589b8f337"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"transmittedMean", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"kLoss", " ", "lossCountLaw"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"kLoss", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "nLoss"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
        RowBox[{"nLoss", ",", " ", "Integers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"nLoss", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[199]:= ",
 CellID->1364978316,ExpressionUUID->"37725419-c8bf-c4cd-5d02-4e42e94bae17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify the mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"n", "\[Eta]"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6eee5857-8f9d-bf63-1696-52112a290249"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->565097818,ExpressionUUID->"2635f536-2fc9-ab3c-4fca-ed704a7df606"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"transmittedMean", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"nLoss", " ", "\[Eta]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{"nLoss", ",", " ", "Integers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"nLoss", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[200]:= ",
 CellID->1520041768,ExpressionUUID->"1b3760e9-4a32-92b2-4acd-79b36fc4e098"],

Cell["Coherent inputs: reduced amplitude and Poisson statistics", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellID->862412655,ExpressionUUID->"14fe93a8-4ee9-5b9e-3c85-0af26a9c29e4"],

Cell["\<\
A coherent input remains coherent under pure loss. Compute its output \
amplitude:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->426217663,ExpressionUUID->"11cf5d11-52cc-ddbb-47f5-555b677ea781"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossCoherentOutput", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"attenuator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", "\[Alpha]Loss", "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[201]:= ",
 CellID->128954499,ExpressionUUID->"7ba8138a-66ce-478c-2957-8ad4137b2dd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its mean photon number becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35c9e6d4-f3c4-84c1-63f6-ff918676ee2b"],
 ". Verify the corresponding vacuum probability:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->731716873,ExpressionUUID->"6fd66644-13e4-6fa7-15ee-782ea591358d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"attenuator", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "\[Alpha]Loss", "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "\[Eta]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Alpha]Loss", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[202]:= ",
 CellID->263464368,ExpressionUUID->"00abf1cf-696b-3507-30a8-e8a9081f9c6d"],

Cell["Finite channels: coherences and repeated attenuation", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->519276129,ExpressionUUID->"03d898fe-d35a-9eef-31e7-11bbe6ece435"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Set the declared transmissivity to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03dda600-4b0b-c3af-31e2-386a6ebf91f5"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1441306302,ExpressionUUID->"4de38b79-ee67-8bee-7b90-23228b13d934"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"halfLoss", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"attenuator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[203]:= ",
 CellID->370920483,ExpressionUUID->"347cf1ed-0cc4-b4dc-5c03-e8b7a5761e26"],

Cell["Draw the resulting device:", "Text",
 CellID->1675734937,ExpressionUUID->"7d81b9ce-3a4c-aa2a-2bbe-30a8bffef970"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"halfLoss", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[204]:= ",
 CellID->1811399761,ExpressionUUID->"6bb9b374-9caf-337d-1946-2b3e155b9e47"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Expose the same map as a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c340229-13f4-0181-15cb-a473a58153eb"],
 " with four Fock levels:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->417262126,ExpressionUUID->"25dfa134-0866-9bb5-53e4-397ea910e99f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossChannel", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"halfLoss", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Channel\>\"", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[205]:= ",
 CellID->1077936938,ExpressionUUID->"425139cc-45a5-cefb-726e-b0966c5194c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Loss also attenuates coherences between photon numbers. Prepare ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      TemplateBox[{"1"},
       "Ket"]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d922994-f334-45bb-7ba1-c0d186c12f81"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->181325614,ExpressionUUID->"06c25578-1780-b25e-2ef2-4d22a23a00a4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossSuperposition", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "I", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "/", 
     
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[206]:= ",
 CellID->2020910698,ExpressionUUID->"5f70617e-b140-9f95-0500-793bc0fae5ff"],

Cell["Apply the channel:", "Text",
 CellID->661155756,ExpressionUUID->"79d0371a-30a6-04e5-2fef-af4441536ecf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossSuperpositionOutput", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"lossChannel", "[", "lossSuperposition", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[207]:= ",
 CellID->1040242161,ExpressionUUID->"7d950d76-dd18-2b24-2baa-a533d4ad760e"],

Cell["Verify normalization of the output:", "Text",
 CellID->758481243,ExpressionUUID->"7234a9f4-3232-6781-23cb-40be47c74deb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lossSuperpositionOutput", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], 
    "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[208]:= ",
 CellID->607101385,ExpressionUUID->"42668d78-f434-72a4-721d-2525fdc1408e"],

Cell["\<\
Verify the density matrix in the occupied vacuum and one-photon sector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->718676885,ExpressionUUID->"0c7cc198-0ad8-2426-3403-d8c2af528f0c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"lossSuperpositionOutput", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], 
     "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{";;", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{";;", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "I"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"I", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[209]:= ",
 CellID->1099629263,ExpressionUUID->"69698b1d-3dc2-3628-1f16-2347b4749d72"],

Cell["\<\
Two pure-loss channels compose by multiplying transmissivities. Apply the \
first half-transmissive stage to three photons:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2120979663,ExpressionUUID->"701e1eb7-eeba-61c8-2025-97f08b4f3312"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"halfLossState", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"halfLoss", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[210]:= ",
 CellID->123468129,ExpressionUUID->"0e322415-281a-3695-37c1-be5f49ac9cff"],

Cell["Apply the second stage to this mixed state:", "Text",
 CellID->513893082,ExpressionUUID->"61beb272-ef15-9663-1745-343f8aa1fd49"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twiceAttenuated", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"halfLoss", "[", "halfLossState", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[211]:= ",
 CellID->1710240506,ExpressionUUID->"5e8a6a96-06b4-6465-0689-83d0b3414f4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify the binomial output with net transmissivity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55951090-ef25-ccfd-03aa-89dd8ad196c7"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1971880122,ExpressionUUID->"53a2ca13-da2c-324e-0151-ec5cdfde8094"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"twiceAttenuated", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ",
   "==", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
   RowBox[{"PDF", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BinomialDistribution", "[", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[212]:= ",
 CellID->482876923,ExpressionUUID->"5930221d-821b-4026-08cf-c44737ae130c"],

Cell["Compose the two QI objects directly:", "Text",
 CellID->257955902,ExpressionUUID->"76ba63e9-5df8-c241-1e5a-7ab3547290ab"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twiceAttenuator", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"halfLoss", "[", "halfLoss", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[213]:= ",
 CellID->1595709984,ExpressionUUID->"319e51f9-a9ce-1d21-67a6-48a2c87b640b"],

Cell["Draw the two loss elements:", "Text",
 CellID->1806165637,ExpressionUUID->"26f4962c-805e-a216-4e8b-087631e8f17c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twiceAttenuator", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[214]:= ",
 CellID->1730622717,ExpressionUUID->"313d5a7b-7caf-7acc-60c3-5c25755a4816"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify the net amplitude factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], "=", "1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2da78195-91be-94f0-5b5c-18df2048feda"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->694790404,ExpressionUUID->"39c6b7ab-78e0-e73c-6ffd-2ef5789aca06"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"twiceAttenuator", "[", "\"\<TransferMatrix\>\"", "]"}], " ", "==", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], "}"}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[215]:= ",
 CellID->1833306836,ExpressionUUID->"3f7d0c35-7157-44bf-6502-a67f00e22e85"],

Cell["Two-photon interference: loss and surviving coincidences", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellID->1703418593,ExpressionUUID->"47b49f91-c3c7-4deb-6d4b-16daf6721731"],

Cell["\<\
Loss can be placed between passive optical elements. With mode mixing, Fock \
occupations must be explicit. Add equal attenuation to both outputs of the \
balanced beam splitter:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1263998950,ExpressionUUID->"064e3005-d89e-7c03-2e75-aa6ed92b4769"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossyHOM", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<Loss\>\"", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<Loss\>\"", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "2"}]}], 
    "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[216]:= ",
 CellID->1096868287,ExpressionUUID->"76c2caed-aea0-13a2-1ef1-e3b6cb556188"],

Cell["Draw the lossy interferometer:", "Text",
 CellID->152289512,ExpressionUUID->"260c3025-1fa9-9acd-4e33-a98f9a5de817"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossyHOM", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[217]:= ",
 CellID->2048354789,ExpressionUUID->"4b1e6c2c-0452-4134-7925-8676ade7101e"],

Cell["Compute the distribution for one photon in each input:", "Text",
 CellID->1927064331,ExpressionUUID->"2982aea8-af87-65d7-5fb1-47f5ca324f3d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossyHOMProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Refine", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"lossyHOM", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[218]:= ",
 CellID->177111739,ExpressionUUID->"19ac3a5e-0cd6-873c-4f53-bc18a560ea06"],

Cell["\<\
Verify normalization, including vacuum and single-photon outcomes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->115596948,ExpressionUUID->"6e8690e9-968f-68b3-16bd-09b3233a3a99"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", "lossyHOMProbabilities", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    "1"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[219]:= ",
 CellID->1114128274,ExpressionUUID->"2b6bc1ec-c569-bd9f-5968-d8c9ec1d07e5"],

Cell["The two-photon coincidence remains suppressed. Verify it:", "Text",
 CellID->1895094918,ExpressionUUID->"25f1a39a-81e0-db80-538e-3ac4379aa9ea"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lossyHOM", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}]}], "]"}], 
  " ", "==", " ", "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[220]:= ",
 CellID->532797841,ExpressionUUID->"35466be2-b7a8-26dc-637d-82cfc2428c26"],

Cell["Sum the probabilities for both photons surviving:", "Text",
 CellID->827514810,ExpressionUUID->"58bdea72-0ba3-5f4c-0842-0c3cae562596"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twoPhotonSurvival", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
   RowBox[{"KeySelect", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lossyHOMProbabilities", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<Name\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "2"}],
       " ", "&"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[221]:= ",
 CellID->1310126569,ExpressionUUID->"6e8cef58-e908-949c-16b3-070588a2fee6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that this probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0abc4047-6c7b-4886-3a44-5a21050e1aec"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1253347759,ExpressionUUID->"24e21d63-fe6b-5877-4c91-954cfb1e2b5d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"twoPhotonSurvival", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[222]:= ",
 CellID->1721654809,ExpressionUUID->"348d2737-4aeb-e3cb-5cb2-bf716e9fb111"],

Cell["\<\
Equal output loss also models equal detector efficiencies before ideal photon \
counting.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1835967532,ExpressionUUID->"2161c865-0900-0907-571e-e24fa8b5586d"],

Cell["Vacuum environment: an independent construction", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->965277466,ExpressionUUID->"3cadbe4b-a339-c651-6452-3014d6cdacbb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Pure loss is equivalent to coupling the signal to a vacuum mode and \
discarding that output. Use a beam splitter with signal transmissivity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31169419-f57b-983b-672d-0e42fc0feb01"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1405388586,ExpressionUUID->"40aa99e8-53bd-499c-70a9-10b266481be6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossDilation", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"ArcCos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "}"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[223]:= ",
 CellID->1630589325,ExpressionUUID->"5d165407-aaf3-867b-0b2e-4e60ce87ed41"],

Cell["Draw the signal and environment modes:", "Text",
 CellID->446366569,ExpressionUUID->"75cb8946-a0dc-0da7-23c8-2123d169578d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossDilation", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[224]:= ",
 CellID->1994518302,ExpressionUUID->"63688a50-35e7-99e6-1117-2c1a4393ebcc"],

Cell["Propagate three signal photons and a vacuum environment:", "Text",
 CellID->1562654637,ExpressionUUID->"12187c95-2034-8b29-4238-75df51c6d673"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"jointLossState", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"lossDilation", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[225]:= ",
 CellID->1372112522,ExpressionUUID->"34b193bd-0a67-a7a6-5c4e-0ae7af130d8c"],

Cell["Trace out environment mode 2:", "Text",
 CellID->638348404,ExpressionUUID->"4fca8ec2-4b73-3b52-75c9-27ac6e0789b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"dilationOutput", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
   RowBox[{"jointLossState", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[226]:= ",
 CellID->907289993,ExpressionUUID->"656925a1-dac3-d209-1316-bc0adf77a153"],

Cell["Verify agreement with the native attenuator:", "Text",
 CellID->1480220716,ExpressionUUID->"09e13884-5cc5-f650-3f9e-b1ee5571dcba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"dilationOutput", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
    " ", "==", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"attenuatedState", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "\[Eta]", " ", "<=", " ", "1"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[227]:= ",
 CellID->1004075994,ExpressionUUID->"29829495-262a-abaa-5fb1-0ddf53dcf9f0"],

Cell["\<\
Four levels per mode retain every sector in these three-photon examples. \
Native loss uses a vacuum environment. Combining loss with squeezing requires \
a Gaussian noise channel and is not supported by QI.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->592936352,ExpressionUUID->"136212ad-a4c2-b9f3-4111-8bf6cd740bd9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Source:", "TI"],
 " Agarwal, Section 5.10, pp. 111-112."
}], "Text",
 CellID->792862978,ExpressionUUID->"67f6b273-a0bf-ee61-0d8d-343cd14bb54b"],

Cell["\<\
13. Waveguide arrays: transport, correlations, and quantum walks\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->573477382,ExpressionUUID->"07a2a6c0-d7ac-3784-2d51-3fade25e9dee"],

Cell["\<\
Coupled waveguides exchange light. Propagation through an array is a passive \
mode transformation, so QI can represent it as an equivalent optical network.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2124988169,ExpressionUUID->"7d29df82-54ab-6c21-24d6-d6ec5d5e370b"],

Cell["Coupled waveguides: continuous photon transport", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->534961831,ExpressionUUID->"2673b224-f5d9-a24c-4e00-2b81fc6df096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Set the nearest-neighbor coupling to one and measure propagation length in \
inverse coupling units. The propagator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27388ee6-22a7-f122-4ec7-27c05753c008"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51cd4bfd-d3fa-9dcf-07f3-62a6e58ce715"],
 " is the single-particle coupling Hamiltonian. Define ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06a776cb-b9d0-3c58-2e5d-6f95386a86a2"],
 " for two waveguides:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->998016997,ExpressionUUID->"7641b941-63e8-8619-1e7e-312b1582ed63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"twoGuideH", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[228]:= ",
 CellID->1107607024,ExpressionUUID->"42b8cf72-fa81-ffe6-7247-e73fff35c5cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the propagator with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MatrixExp",
   BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
   ButtonData->{
     URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/MatrixExp.html"], 
     None}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1c8db7a0-3aa3-299f-44b2-2e0abf567be5"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1668318198,ExpressionUUID->"473593be-64fb-e664-6eca-0af80c8fcd4e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twoGuidePropagator", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "couplingLength", " ", "twoGuideH"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[229]:= ",
 CellID->1044073123,ExpressionUUID->"79a8e286-b760-8808-2f57-fbe3c21adb52"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build the equivalent beam splitter with reflection phase ",
 Cell["-\\[Pi]/2", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "766f3dde-6e6e-8ae3-1e14-b4980b18d8c9"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1281286378,ExpressionUUID->"7acff19c-f8f8-c05b-2af4-e8d9f97292a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twoGuideSplitter", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"couplingLength", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "\[Pi]"}], "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[230]:= ",
 CellID->2002157654,ExpressionUUID->"36bb0aa4-099e-3511-5e58-a30ea8289c7b"],

Cell["Draw the equivalent beam splitter:", "Text",
 CellID->822148062,ExpressionUUID->"6fab4322-7f5b-c123-15a9-5a8c7aef9009"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"twoGuideSplitter", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[231]:= ",
 CellID->837975234,ExpressionUUID->"559c0528-76f1-864e-03a3-9d720285ec94"],

Cell["\<\
Verify agreement between the Hamiltonian propagator and beam splitter \
transfer matrix:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2104272152,ExpressionUUID->"4c3b3e9a-7f95-6e09-75d8-b7c47a203553"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"twoGuidePropagator", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"twoGuideSplitter", "[", "\"\<Unitary\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"couplingLength", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[232]:= ",
 CellID->39229099,ExpressionUUID->"7b834648-1855-f17e-29b1-581299e1c044"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The negative reflection phase matches the sign in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6aa15cf4-f328-f435-1a5f-55b186c2df1f"],
 ". For a larger array, compute the propagator numerically before \
constructing QI's optical mesh. Symbolic parameters remain available in \
element-based constructions."
}], "Text",
 CellID->538455469,ExpressionUUID->"1fa3178e-7287-38be-4550-8ee807338a84"],

Cell["\<\
Construct the nearest-neighbor Hamiltonian for five waveguides:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->266517012,ExpressionUUID->"33c53063-afff-c489-61fa-aa4cc98baed3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"arrayHamiltonian", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Band", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Band", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}],
       "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[233]:= ",
 CellID->1190814367,ExpressionUUID->"08d8bcb3-70a4-55b3-38e7-35fd01513f99"],

Cell["Verify that the array Hamiltonian is Hermitian:", "Text",
 CellID->1899183568,ExpressionUUID->"20e38226-5aed-155d-5090-1b805e987fa7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"HermitianMatrixQ", "[", "arrayHamiltonian", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[234]:= ",
 CellID->839992789,ExpressionUUID->"160727ef-d1b8-0069-3e3c-bec8e04d52b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the equivalent optical network at numerical propagation length ",
 Cell[BoxData["length"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "261df1b1-b81e-57af-4e22-e8fb39ab3df5"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1909137676,ExpressionUUID->"00ba9d2f-c328-50fc-3059-1488f6dd22c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"arrayDevice", "[", 
   RowBox[{"length_", "?", "NumericQ"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"N", "[", 
    RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "length", " ", "arrayHamiltonian"}], "]"}], 
    "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[235]:= ",
 CellID->2000873505,ExpressionUUID->"02964792-f196-8b6e-32ae-5edf8020d9b4"],

Cell["Construct the network at unit propagation length:", "Text",
 CellID->1091748765,ExpressionUUID->"166d4e5f-4333-9385-3e13-601976c7e1ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"arrayAtOne", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"arrayDevice", "[", "1", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[236]:= ",
 CellID->232863170,ExpressionUUID->"1c99ee20-d785-d362-44a6-078de231be48"],

Cell["Draw its equivalent beam splitter mesh:", "Text",
 CellID->1876092091,ExpressionUUID->"60858f89-56d8-6615-10ba-26d3636d4d7f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"arrayAtOne", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[237]:= ",
 CellID->652142632,ExpressionUUID->"2e45545e-c429-efe4-567b-4e1bedddb5ce"],

Cell["Read the transfer matrix:", "Text",
 CellID->330963574,ExpressionUUID->"24564246-a2b2-7a9b-4c6e-6423d74748e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"arrayMatrix", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"arrayAtOne", "[", "\"\<Unitary\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[238]:= ",
 CellID->1389046362,ExpressionUUID->"273d1382-afb1-09c0-4ec2-8aefca445b2a"],

Cell["Verify that the array transfer matrix is unitary:", "Text",
 CellID->1332526183,ExpressionUUID->"39c9e52f-ed06-87fb-6ff6-fc8884b0edc1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"UnitaryMatrixQ", "[", "arrayMatrix", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[239]:= ",
 CellID->197217751,ExpressionUUID->"46be6341-4be3-06d9-6e46-7b2b6d966c23"],

Cell["Construct the zero-length network:", "Text",
 CellID->880034747,ExpressionUUID->"352b8971-1d3f-d4c9-6328-213b94cbbe13"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"arrayAtZero", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"arrayDevice", "[", "0", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[240]:= ",
 CellID->1800574979,ExpressionUUID->"227c7e4b-1c68-aac8-5204-70159502f812"],

Cell["Draw its uncoupled modes:", "Text",
 CellID->1078219960,ExpressionUUID->"6cd9b5a9-dbed-51da-14e6-2cf2dd982320"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"arrayAtZero", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[241]:= ",
 CellID->2033801793,ExpressionUUID->"4becebe3-5bfe-fac0-7993-02cd5d88c82a"],

Cell["Verify the identity transfer matrix at zero length:", "Text",
 CellID->1670899349,ExpressionUUID->"312d182f-c6c7-5e1e-60d2-9188f3722564"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"arrayAtZero", "[", "\"\<Unitary\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "5", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[242]:= ",
 CellID->975439503,ExpressionUUID->"1449d45f-8382-90b9-3c76-ce193634e283"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the single-photon output probabilities for the central input:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->351741581,ExpressionUUID->"444f09dd-766a-dba7-6c74-a087031ca98d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"arraySingleProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"arrayAtOne", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Probability\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], 
        "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"UnitVector", "[", 
        RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[243]:= ",
 CellID->984679481,ExpressionUUID->"79e9b65a-67eb-1624-2f96-2804119e7d0e"],

Cell["\<\
Verify agreement with the squared moduli of the third transfer-matrix column:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->412548195,ExpressionUUID->"394df0e2-3b3f-7a44-6f72-e9ccbeca48ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arraySingleProbabilities", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"arrayMatrix", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], 
    "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[244]:= ",
 CellID->167190678,ExpressionUUID->"5d3de1d4-e864-19c9-04c2-f89189116b13"],

Cell["\<\
Reflection symmetry requires a symmetric distribution. Verify it:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->132154406,ExpressionUUID->"1adc8861-0296-99d3-4ae3-224bb720eb39"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arraySingleProbabilities", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", "arraySingleProbabilities", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[245]:= ",
 CellID->1448639745,ExpressionUUID->"47f3727e-1788-b883-6d81-7438a2220ae9"],

Cell["\<\
Verify normalization of the single-photon output distribution:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1881657070,ExpressionUUID->"02bfa0ec-e0fe-2fa7-3244-39c9908b758d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", "arraySingleProbabilities", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    "1"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[246]:= ",
 CellID->1506900826,ExpressionUUID->"7cc1833e-1ead-5711-24fe-1b789b583a7b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A coherent input reproduces the same spatial profile in its mean output \
photon numbers. Send symbolic coherent amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Alpha]Array"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cb4236e-91b2-9328-644b-bb482044fe72"],
 " into the central waveguide:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->637363640,ExpressionUUID->"631da35c-735e-7e3b-1122-3b0606eb4501"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"arrayClassicalField", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"arrayAtOne", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Coherent\>\"", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]Array", " ", 
     RowBox[{"UnitVector", "[", 
      RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[247]:= ",
 CellID->658697144,ExpressionUUID->"44b7daea-ed84-b50e-6c4c-d3b784361c54"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mean output photon numbers equal the single-photon probabilities times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39f2334d-24de-3dcb-6f81-ab174d688711"],
 ". Verify this relation, using ",
 Cell[BoxData["Chop"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ec600b7-0050-8550-46fd-99f1b1eaefba"],
 " for numerical residuals:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->462592558,ExpressionUUID->"33bfe66e-cd59-d601-6144-f84be4edbd6b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"First", "[", "arrayClassicalField", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], 
     " ", "-", "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Alpha]Array", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
      "arraySingleProbabilities"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[248]:= ",
 CellID->621689956,ExpressionUUID->"6a3ee8c1-8740-e1ad-1bc5-01ab32fab3f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Mean photon numbers do not describe two-photon correlations. The normally \
ordered correlation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33885b0f-111a-0c54-6188-5369a0af56be"],
 " counts ordered detection pairs. Compute the output distribution for \
photons entering waveguides two and four:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->912512294,ExpressionUUID->"5c9080a8-67dd-9047-04af-19f21269e2ad"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"arrayPairProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"arrayAtOne", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[249]:= ",
 CellID->159314101,ExpressionUUID->"2abc9d06-0494-496b-5a43-1560ad211bb1"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the correlation matrix by averaging over occupation patterns:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2072053663,ExpressionUUID->"43e301a0-76bb-1057-7190-980a034e62bd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"arrayCorrelations", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<Name\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"#2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "n", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], " ", "-",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", "n", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], 
       " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", " ", "arrayPairProbabilities"}], "]"}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[250]:= ",
 CellID->1700462496,ExpressionUUID->"1ae06f2b-7109-3ba5-4a9f-877500bd898f"],

Cell["\<\
Two photons give two ordered pairs. Verify that the matrix entries sum to two:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->758245071,ExpressionUUID->"0856a555-3f58-6085-386d-3d1fbaed32ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{"arrayCorrelations", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    "2"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[251]:= ",
 CellID->645457834,ExpressionUUID->"71eecbe3-9be0-9ba6-2795-e2cd1d9ae98c"],

Cell["Plot the two-photon correlation matrix:", "Text",
 CellID->1053805191,ExpressionUUID->"59070895-187c-42ea-0f3c-a1df99091030"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ArrayPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"arrayCorrelations", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Output mode\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Output mode\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Two photons propagating through five coupled waveguides\>\""}], 
   ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "380"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[252]:= ",
 CellID->1335228883,ExpressionUUID->"189fe470-6cd8-7cf4-48a4-fe3a056d46de"],

Cell["\<\
QI can sample without first enumerating the full distribution. Here we \
compare sample frequencies with the distribution already calculated. Set a \
reproducible seed:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->17162129,ExpressionUUID->"04ed2843-d86c-272a-2c92-c22cd91e8a70"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "23", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[253]:= ",
 CellID->745178489,ExpressionUUID->"70d9e217-b7c7-416b-20e6-0450c27213b1"],

Cell["Draw three thousand samples from the two-photon input:", "Text",
 CellID->64377810,ExpressionUUID->"29221b72-bc55-8ef4-58d1-933c35e1d4de"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"arraySampleCounts", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"arrayAtOne", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<SampleCounts\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], 
      "}"}], ",", " ", "3000"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[254]:= ",
 CellID->1276099438,ExpressionUUID->"41172bde-c012-830e-772c-c29bf1a4ee54"],

Cell["Verify the number of samples:", "Text",
 CellID->1651008988,ExpressionUUID->"3dd84232-0c35-660d-6bf8-647ca5c04d57"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Total", "[", "arraySampleCounts", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "3000"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[255]:= ",
 CellID->807143410,ExpressionUUID->"5558c8fc-3d33-9e90-0367-e1a6b4c7e4fa"],

Cell["Convert the sample counts to relative frequencies:", "Text",
 CellID->2004841178,ExpressionUUID->"53291d47-a111-bd44-02d6-9520d0a507ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"arrayFrequencies", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"arraySampleCounts", "/", "3000"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[256]:= ",
 CellID->680262370,ExpressionUUID->"14460f59-6b0f-818e-3c7d-a7030ebbd3d4"],

Cell["\<\
Subtract the frequencies from the predicted probabilities by occupation \
pattern:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2074260939,ExpressionUUID->"6afe19ed-5a5e-331e-1a85-90b75fe89e64"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"arrayFrequencyDifferences", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Merge", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"arrayPairProbabilities", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "arrayFrequencies"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Total"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[257]:= ",
 CellID->1484886568,ExpressionUUID->"142f588d-e120-bc70-3dd5-51d690da075a"],

Cell["Compute the largest absolute frequency difference:", "Text",
 CellID->1547996435,ExpressionUUID->"029948d8-232c-2201-32a7-618256d9716b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Values", "[", "arrayFrequencyDifferences", "]"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[258]:= ",
 CellID->1622616291,ExpressionUUID->"4b1b5b6f-b43d-594b-7939-53493dc82b91"],

Cell["\<\
This error fluctuates between runs. Increase the sample size to explore its \
dependence on the number of samples.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1371263066,ExpressionUUID->"32f703b9-71e1-95eb-628c-9ae30795ff31"],

Cell["Discrete-time quantum walks: coupling position and direction", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellID->1067912469,ExpressionUUID->"0c860bbc-8d1f-f590-34bd-a2e624abdffa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A discrete-time quantum walk alternates a ",
 StyleBox["coin operation",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", which mixes two internal states, with a shift conditioned on the coin \
state. Here two optical modes at each position encode the coin states: one \
moves left and the other right."
}], "Text",
 CellID->943837838,ExpressionUUID->"1bab88a0-6539-d521-49a8-210a0ccdbc0b"],

Cell["\<\
Use nine positions with periodic boundaries. From the center, four steps \
cannot wrap around, so the result also describes four steps on an infinite \
line. Define the positions:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1450235700,ExpressionUUID->"74b37722-3fdc-1a4f-1c41-6e8cba696895"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"walkPositions", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "4"}], ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[259]:= ",
 CellID->257312343,ExpressionUUID->"31781dc2-1028-33d4-6707-94aca1c2813e"],

Cell["Define the Hadamard coin operation:", "Text",
 CellID->1811882128,ExpressionUUID->"2148b02c-d62e-5336-5777-2989e3db3e1c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"walkCoin", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[260]:= ",
 CellID->33577298,ExpressionUUID->"183293a6-0d60-7813-49c1-0a00a4154b79"],

Cell["Construct the conditional shift with periodic boundaries:", "Text",
 CellID->240192060,ExpressionUUID->"61e1f3c1-eae0-3799-179e-eaaa8e9a9de3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"walkShift", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"RotateLeft", "[", 
       RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "9", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", 
    "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"RotateRight", "[", 
       RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "9", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[261]:= ",
 CellID->1178070921,ExpressionUUID->"20bddc2d-650e-8031-5042-d6770cb8d31b"],

Cell["Apply the coin operation before the shift to form one step:", "Text",
 CellID->1900683911,ExpressionUUID->"7a437910-f355-55ba-2a71-715d86e03f80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"walkStep", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"walkShift", " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "9", "]"}], ",", " ", "walkCoin"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[262]:= ",
 CellID->760242175,ExpressionUUID->"49429438-4a3e-974e-7f71-0e626fc8fd94"],

Cell["Verify that one step is unitary:", "Text",
 CellID->828244791,ExpressionUUID->"07e2168c-1726-1a27-2d91-8fd6a2d3690d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"UnitaryMatrixQ", "[", "walkStep", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[263]:= ",
 CellID->338384234,ExpressionUUID->"3540c51c-f580-c338-637f-dd59fc3aae02"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Modes 9 and 10 encode the two coin states at position zero. Prepare a \
relative phase of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "684f0173-fe99-1571-1874-993cfb2c7c5b"],
 " to obtain a symmetric position distribution. Build the preparation beam \
splitter:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->455054057,ExpressionUUID->"6e32c5a8-aee9-5273-17c1-dcf5ca9c2159"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"walkPreparation", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<BS\>\"", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"9", ",", " ", "10"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "18"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[264]:= ",
 CellID->1632384583,ExpressionUUID->"607492e2-157b-ba0c-100b-0bcc9c0f0956"],

Cell["Draw the preparation network:", "Text",
 CellID->1806839179,ExpressionUUID->"7781757c-388d-abb9-1dbf-6d26b939f983"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"walkPreparation", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[265]:= ",
 CellID->1374498314,ExpressionUUID->"566e7348-207a-dc95-7e16-6b12510ca6ff"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the transfer matrix for preparation followed by four walk steps:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1735539757,ExpressionUUID->"39672ae7-82f4-b353-6f1c-c3c1368601b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"walkTransfer", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixPower", "[", 
     RowBox[{"walkStep", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"walkPreparation", "[", "\"\<Unitary\>\"", "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[266]:= ",
 CellID->913947365,ExpressionUUID->"0c48aba4-6f27-6a39-3477-420e0ad23903"],

Cell["Construct the equivalent optical network from this matrix:", "Text",
 CellID->33048482,ExpressionUUID->"2f62374d-f3df-131c-5511-af16866a7e66"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"walkDevice", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"N", "[", "walkTransfer", "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[267]:= ",
 CellID->1913442451,ExpressionUUID->"455ea632-3d4d-f0d3-7365-387cb4f9c239"],

Cell["Draw the eighteen-mode network:", "Text",
 CellID->1066460469,ExpressionUUID->"1f0fb95c-030e-c889-4534-3106b6b89ad3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"walkDevice", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "1000"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[268]:= ",
 CellID->1552927865,ExpressionUUID->"16268eae-a572-7912-3fdd-270bcc074878"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the output distribution for a photon entering mode 9:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->262489656,ExpressionUUID->"346a0e1a-2221-987e-5c69-a04457d5eb44"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"walkProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"walkDevice", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Probabilities\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"UnitVector", "[", 
      RowBox[{"18", ",", " ", "9"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[269]:= ",
 CellID->409171113,ExpressionUUID->"366be24c-537a-43bb-5e68-0416660f1181"],

Cell["\<\
Sum over the two coin states at each position to obtain the position \
distribution:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->189753264,ExpressionUUID->"501b1457-1a1d-907b-0038-8e119fa9e341"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"walkPositionProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
   RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"Total", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<Name\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}],
         ")"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "walkProbabilities"}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[270]:= ",
 CellID->1113565082,ExpressionUUID->"291c68e0-f532-6cdd-5f23-81cdfcc73627"],

Cell["Verify normalization after summing over the coin states:", "Text",
 CellID->474827638,ExpressionUUID->"5c29c458-c353-7b98-05d6-de05f6e649e2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", "walkPositionProbabilities", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    "1"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[271]:= ",
 CellID->480943277,ExpressionUUID->"6e1a2d6a-d2ad-c32a-1639-c537e759ae70"],

Cell["\<\
Verify reflection symmetry of the walk's position distribution:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->19659169,ExpressionUUID->"6eb5612b-2266-f0f1-164b-79755710c2db"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{"walkPositionProbabilities", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", "walkPositionProbabilities", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[272]:= ",
 CellID->1122889797,ExpressionUUID->"1f4b4965-e043-b514-4549-614e91f71c7e"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the position distribution for a four-step classical unbiased random \
walk:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1606600295,ExpressionUUID->"5bf36e21-2d79-2b6f-0980-878b440c79b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"classicalPositionProbabilities", " ", "=", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"PDF", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"BinomialDistribution", "[", 
     RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "+", " ", "walkPositions"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[273]:= ",
 CellID->215661095,ExpressionUUID->"6fe9f85b-1ce6-27f0-1596-f20594908dda"],

Cell["\<\
The classical walk adds path probabilities; the quantum walk adds path \
amplitudes. Pair each position with its probability for both walks:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1518204824,ExpressionUUID->"3eadea9f-7d43-757d-6652-03d974f65c47"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"walkPlotData", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"walkPositions", ",", " ", "#"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
    " ", "/@", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "walkPositionProbabilities", ",", " ", 
      "classicalPositionProbabilities"}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[274]:= ",
 CellID->1890580947,ExpressionUUID->"68be2dd2-eea3-f2cb-1845-c49f8b57c011"],

Cell["Compare the two position distributions:", "Text",
 CellID->1680570408,ExpressionUUID->"1279eb8d-ef8a-5dbb-4206-02d68a3f2781"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"walkPlotData", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Position\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Probability\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Quantum walk\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Classical walk\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Four-step position distributions\>\""}], 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[275]:= ",
 CellID->475458560,ExpressionUUID->"6afb4307-9f81-9d1b-1a99-5b611a35e461"],

Cell["\<\
Summing over the coin states preserves the interference accumulated during \
propagation. Increase the position range when adding steps to avoid the \
periodic boundary.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->823056013,ExpressionUUID->"2e902be9-4fb4-3e90-56af-c2b36a4684fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Source:", "TI"],
 " Agarwal, Sections 19.1-19.3 and 19.5, pp. 432-442 and 447-452."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1392600812,ExpressionUUID->"46e8ad28-93a4-355d-6e97-457226569fa7"],

Cell["\<\
14. Conditional optical gates: implementing a nonlinear sign change\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1250002485,ExpressionUUID->"43090fa7-5002-8b65-7136-a60161b4d64f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A phase shifter multiplies an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d6689b0-bbf9-a698-3b1d-20fa3d8d0ce2"],
 "-photon Fock state by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"i", "n", "\[Phi]"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ac87485-b214-a6e0-7ac8-6deec7a60cca"],
 ". Build a one-mode phase shifter with a symbolic phase:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1196503608,ExpressionUUID->"56e1d4b5-6b25-2976-7e9e-cdff0ed0785c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ordinaryPhase", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<PS\>\"", "[", "phaseNS", "]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[276]:= ",
 CellID->35509309,ExpressionUUID->"2e41722a-1026-02f0-567f-7474a1d350da"],

Cell["Draw the phase shifter:", "Text",
 CellID->133207102,ExpressionUUID->"6aacec8a-85e6-bbaa-1a53-05d4339009f0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ordinaryPhase", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<Diagram\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ShowParameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[277]:= ",
 CellID->1619111818,ExpressionUUID->"1c51a735-fee5-6802-446e-3f7efa903b68"],

Cell["\<\
Compute its amplitude, assuming a nonnegative integer photon number:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1609727223,ExpressionUUID->"5e54a15d-ecde-9aa9-066b-39068568e8f3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"phaseAmplitude", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Refine", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ordinaryPhase", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", "phasePhotons", "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "phasePhotons", "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{"phasePhotons", ",", " ", "Integers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"phasePhotons", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[278]:= ",
 CellID->550162028,ExpressionUUID->"27fb6428-ecec-27d4-4d99-7e75849e8d3e"],

Cell["Verify the photon-number phase law:", "Text",
 CellID->1908615943,ExpressionUUID->"51f5ca74-88a2-9d2c-078a-ec3e2954e476"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"phaseAmplitude", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{"I", " ", "phasePhotons", " ", "phaseNS"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{"phasePhotons", ",", " ", "Integers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"phasePhotons", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"phaseNS", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[279]:= ",
 CellID->1143006314,ExpressionUUID->"1154648e-ef0b-aa2b-476c-7deb8abff971"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At phase ",
 Cell["\\[Pi]/2", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "4c057904-8649-af2b-743b-716e33fdf271"],
 ", read the vacuum, one-photon, and two-photon amplitudes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1196348210,ExpressionUUID->"2baf9433-2e90-ebaf-5954-0e7d4b2ab9f5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"phaseAmplitude", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"phaseNS", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"phasePhotons", " ", "->", " ", "n"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[280]:= ",
 CellID->742714341,ExpressionUUID->"340e6ec8-e38f-b030-5c35-8795963b031a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two-photon amplitude changes sign, but the one-photon amplitude also \
changes. A ",
 StyleBox["nonlinear sign gate",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " instead maps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "0"], 
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "1"], 
    TemplateBox[{"1"},
     "Ket"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "2"], 
    TemplateBox[{"2"},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64bff79f-1679-3ebc-0c44-eed9a30d8486"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "0"], 
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "1"], 
    TemplateBox[{"1"},
     "Ket"]}], "-", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "2"], 
    TemplateBox[{"2"},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "126dc52b-3dd5-bd31-4212-dd75b461041b"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1675247856,ExpressionUUID->"28023c0b-10a3-7000-5831-b655a156436a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Linear optics can implement this gate conditionally with auxiliary photons \
and heralding. Mode 1 carries the signal; modes 2 and 3 contain one photon \
and vacuum. Success requires the same auxiliary output occupation pattern ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f1b960d-0301-b7cd-7538-0857b6b51d17"],
 ". Construct the three-mode transfer matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->288968408,ExpressionUUID->"268b8fe7-2cf2-fa64-4e88-26c14484c94e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nsMatrix", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"3", "/", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "4"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"3", "/", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[281]:= ",
 CellID->1029027830,ExpressionUUID->"41763b34-5a53-ec31-770d-b37e5fe7b71b"],

Cell["The matrix is real. Verify unitarity using its transpose:", "Text",
 CellID->128002051,ExpressionUUID->"5d61c4f4-c0fb-847a-0b1e-ddb1f08fef40"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"RootReduce", "[", 
   RowBox[{"nsMatrix", " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "nsMatrix", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[282]:= ",
 CellID->1571712410,ExpressionUUID->"72fe9a0c-0c49-239f-2285-1c56a5fc71e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The selected transition amplitude is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", "1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"0", GridBox[{
       {
        StyleBox["U", "TI"]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14bcbead-0cb8-f132-3c43-37f7a532c018"],
 ". Photon-number conservation preserves the signal photon number on success. \
Build the network from the transfer matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->890139439,ExpressionUUID->"4a015340-38cc-91ca-7a3f-4b2ab97ee310"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsGate", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumInterferometer", "[", "nsMatrix", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[283]:= ",
 CellID->999332945,ExpressionUUID->"44807b7f-366d-41a7-6cb0-73394318138d"],

Cell["Draw the network before heralding:", "Text",
 CellID->662631669,ExpressionUUID->"56b5d630-2397-dc8b-7e4a-c87a5623a6d1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsGate", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[284]:= ",
 CellID->798789937,ExpressionUUID->"066e8396-42fa-b64f-2e15-1ad0768c1c95"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the selected transition amplitudes for signal photon numbers zero, \
one, and two:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->647724388,ExpressionUUID->"0fee4e15-659c-ade9-3596-605f0c2ef733"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsAmplitudes", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"RootReduce", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"nsGate", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[285]:= ",
 CellID->1693391218,ExpressionUUID->"6f99faa1-7599-adaa-15a6-f30b7c2df7f0"],

Cell["Verify the amplitude vector for the nonlinear sign gate:", "Text",
 CellID->819462336,ExpressionUUID->"6c80f068-193e-1d5a-14bf-ea3298cb67a0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsAmplitudes", " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}], "/", "2"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[286]:= ",
 CellID->1116629832,ExpressionUUID->"77601adb-bf25-4789-1d1f-93853ad02dd3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The common amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48b830c7-d270-6a57-7847-a9a0e70538bd"],
 " gives success probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62f1d7f5-6807-0c72-128e-cebf09b25758"],
 " for every normalized input in the gate subspace. Verify this for arbitrary \
complex coefficients:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->871366443,ExpressionUUID->"1e2af966-75ba-f15e-4629-f1407c4cc3a4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"nsAmplitudes", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"c0", ",", " ", "c1", ",", " ", "c2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "^", 
      "2"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"c0", ",", " ", "c1", ",", " ", "c2"}], "}"}], "]"}], "^", 
      "2"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[287]:= ",
 CellID->1498962183,ExpressionUUID->"7fcb302b-9e92-9019-25c8-aa751b24e363"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Check the full state evolution and heralding projection. Four levels per \
mode retain all sectors because the total input photon number is at most \
three. Prepare the signal with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["c", "TI"], "0"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["c", "TI"], "1"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["c", "TI"], "2"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "=", "1"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "361ba0ac-b25b-03c3-5e38-3909c7ee5129"],
 ", declaring its coefficients for later substitution:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->914693011,ExpressionUUID->"36c5768f-9366-0c29-5efb-6fe926135773"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsSignal", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"c0", ",", " ", "c1", ",", " ", "c2", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",",
     " ", "4", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"c0", ",", " ", "c1", ",", " ", "c2"}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[288]:= ",
 CellID->2145390693,ExpressionUUID->"43fcd6d4-594a-1482-7183-cf9e58ff7ee8"],

Cell["Add the one-photon and vacuum auxiliary inputs:", "Text",
 CellID->272231904,ExpressionUUID->"4719bc21-ede2-73f0-6d26-358a8b9741da"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsInput", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
   RowBox[{"nsSignal", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[289]:= ",
 CellID->183385376,ExpressionUUID->"71a147e0-ad25-39c0-275f-5ecdc4d18b2a"],

Cell["Propagate the full input state:", "Text",
 CellID->1323839713,ExpressionUUID->"0d94734f-f5fd-5b1e-3bac-6b2883882664"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsOutput", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nsGate", "[", "nsInput", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[290]:= ",
 CellID->1299720858,ExpressionUUID->"4a66d044-93ea-cfa5-7a1d-ca2e259c958f"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that propagation preserves the parameter declarations:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->513341225,ExpressionUUID->"08e3a6ae-198b-2f89-3890-3f08983e75d3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nsOutput", "[", "\"\<ParameterSpec\>\"", "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nsInput", "[", "\"\<ParameterSpec\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[291]:= ",
 CellID->2063978445,ExpressionUUID->"07ff9e3d-196e-b566-2d84-106798181c4c"],

Cell["\<\
Reshape the output amplitudes so the three indices label the three modes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->124947567,ExpressionUUID->"7611561e-6aa4-cbf1-1e2f-48580f5699db"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nsOutputTensor", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
      RowBox[{"nsOutput", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[292]:= ",
 CellID->307500845,ExpressionUUID->"6d91ad73-9dce-768e-1bae-453d147b5cd4"],

Cell["\<\
Auxiliary photon numbers one and zero select indices two and one. Extract the \
unnormalized conditional signal vector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->971031069,ExpressionUUID->"6bff65fb-5d0a-196c-1985-7ca554bf6bb6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nsSelected", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"nsOutputTensor", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[293]:= ",
 CellID->959838422,ExpressionUUID->"5e58ca76-8595-5ac4-0667-ec302c20282e"],

Cell["Verify the conditional vector before normalization:", "Text",
 CellID->1887610507,ExpressionUUID->"08a91809-3406-7705-3856-9253bdb35a6f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"nsSelected", " ", "==", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"c0", ",", " ", "c1", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"-", "c2"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "/", "2"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[294]:= ",
 CellID->1384833740,ExpressionUUID->"47ee4125-d524-d464-6d96-588edcd6bf4e"],

Cell["Compute the success probability:", "Text",
 CellID->1880473289,ExpressionUUID->"1a0bea5a-c3ff-c671-4a08-0c07f58bad5b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nsSuccess", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "nsSelected", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[295]:= ",
 CellID->117881571,ExpressionUUID->"2d2ec88d-5e53-28f6-54d5-e1d75be67adc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify success probability ",
 Cell["1/4", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "230fc3bf-d3e5-5aa5-5134-daf8e590288f"],
 " for every normalized input in the gate subspace:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->372521314,ExpressionUUID->"0c6e076f-8b93-3c10-3415-9f492e27877a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nsSuccess", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"c0", ",", " ", "c1", ",", " ", "c2"}], "}"}], "]"}], "^", 
      "2"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[296]:= ",
 CellID->1020330751,ExpressionUUID->"29094997-c9cb-f733-5f37-60d0e87fda19"],

Cell["\<\
Normalize the selected vector and carry its parameter declarations into the \
conditional state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->339737350,ExpressionUUID->"284fc6fb-b6ce-6422-5874-dfa4c37b4f08"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsConditionalState", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"nsSelected", "/", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "nsSuccess", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "4", ",", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<ParameterSpec\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"nsOutput", "[", "\"\<ParameterSpec\>\"", "]"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[297]:= ",
 CellID->967879197,ExpressionUUID->"0cad16aa-0a89-b805-3452-8ff4af3d0b6f"],

Cell["\<\
Read the conditional state vector under the input normalization constraint:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2045221242,ExpressionUUID->"5640583a-c911-1fe8-7e70-5267e8a46532"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
    RowBox[{"nsConditionalState", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"c0", ",", " ", "c1", ",", " ", "c2"}], "}"}], "]"}], "^", 
      "2"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[298]:= ",
 CellID->2119433676,ExpressionUUID->"6944803a-8297-e066-1f7b-1a643723b34c"],

Cell["Verify normalization of the conditional state:", "Text",
 CellID->1666150564,ExpressionUUID->"7e9e495e-a796-7cd0-26a6-611bd223463a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"nsConditionalState", "[", "\"\<Norm\>\"", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    "1"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"c0", ",", " ", "c1", ",", " ", "c2"}], "}"}], "]"}], "^", 
      "2"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[299]:= ",
 CellID->664696531,ExpressionUUID->"534f7e63-03c8-ee33-0175-704db662b519"],

Cell["\<\
Bind a normalized complex input through the conditional state's parameter \
interface:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->79098559,ExpressionUUID->"3b07ad27-9e6a-154b-693c-44811b1f7f91"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsExampleState", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nsConditionalState", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"<|", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"c0", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"c1", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", "/", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"c2", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}]}], "|>"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[300]:= ",
 CellID->923612531,ExpressionUUID->"1c7a415c-3e53-b7cb-441a-5906bbe71d11"],

Cell["Verify that the two-photon coefficient changes sign:", "Text",
 CellID->725718587,ExpressionUUID->"417aec05-2fbb-8238-7719-066f4a4fd102"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
    RowBox[{"nsExampleState", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}],
   " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "I", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "3", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[301]:= ",
 CellID->868291647,ExpressionUUID->"4705486f-1ac0-4964-6d3b-62499f75184e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The output coefficients are proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "I", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3af5a034-7641-6879-6a8a-3a7e03f43b43"],
 ", as required. The gate is defined only on signal photon numbers zero \
through two. Compute the selected transition amplitude for a three-photon \
signal:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->986753062,ExpressionUUID->"68379bed-79e9-22be-19cc-12b77f9c7084"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nsBeyondAmplitude", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"RootReduce", "[", 
   RowBox[{"nsGate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[302]:= ",
 CellID->1712489022,ExpressionUUID->"460eb9f9-c41e-8ef4-6e35-30a2eda8d4de"],

Cell["Verify that it differs from both gate amplitudes:", "Text",
 CellID->1130883020,ExpressionUUID->"258251be-7c16-7495-53b2-48f875a35eff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nsBeyondAmplitude", " ", "!=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], " ", "&&", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nsBeyondAmplitude", " ", "!=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "2"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[303]:= ",
 CellID->826918846,ExpressionUUID->"35c1f832-722b-ca69-63fe-f27c07df98b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Source:", "TI"],
 " Kok and Lovett, ",
 StyleBox["Introduction to Optical Quantum Information Processing", "TI"],
 ", Section 6.2.2, Exercise 6.4 and Figure 6.5, pp. 183-186. QI computes the \
unitary evolution; projection onto the heralding outcome gives the \
conditional gate."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1119720649,ExpressionUUID->"7b6a50da-eb07-3910-296a-49878eb3887a"],

Cell["Scope and further experiments", "Subsection",
 CellID->747338226,ExpressionUUID->"23591dbb-79d4-ec10-5166-94e57866b77a"],

Cell["\<\
QI supports lossless passive and squeezed networks, and passive networks with \
pure loss. Lossy devices provide Fock probabilities, pure coherent outputs, \
finite-state propagation, and finite channels. Symbolic occupations work for \
lossless passive transition queries and independent attenuators. Mode mixing \
with loss requires explicit occupations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1214057513,ExpressionUUID->"114fd905-c79d-9420-4774-d16ef229ff0a"],

Cell["\<\
Loss with squeezing, lossy Fock transition amplitudes, and lossy sampling are \
unsupported. Mixed Fock/coherent transition inputs require lossless passive \
optics. A Gaussian state specified only by its mean vector and covariance \
matrix is not a native input; its Fock-space representation can use the \
finite-state route.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1068045466,ExpressionUUID->"0047a90f-9cb0-808d-307c-4169154ad2d7"],

Cell["\<\
Thermal environments, homodyne detection, temporal wave-packet overlap, dark \
counts, and adaptive feed-forward require additional modeling. Change one \
input, optical parameter, or heralding outcome at a time, then rerun the \
normalization and limiting-case checks.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->207361811,ExpressionUUID->"42e32fd7-26e6-6b71-7290-c6915293365b"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"4a2652ed-88d4-efb2-7bde-4bb72966b598"
]
